{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real","id":115780,"title":"Idigam Chronicles weekly discussion: Gifts (this time for real)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-19T04:26:35-07:00","id":115780,"title":"Idigam Chronicles weekly discussion: Gifts (this time for real)","content":"Stew's comments and several first draft examples. Let discussion begin! From the writer's point of view, we're very excited by this new approach. Chris has done a fantastic job!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 04-19-2014, 07:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T04:45:21-07:00","id":115786,"title":"","content":"I know that I'm excited about them, but I'm looking forward to fan response. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T04:52:39-07:00","id":115790,"title":"","content":"Those are <i>awesome</i>. I almost did a spit take that all Elodoths have near-perfect scene-long truth detection <i>that counts lies of omission, half-truths or dissembling</i>. And some of the moon gifts can nicely turn a hunt into something out of a horror movie,shutting down lights and means of communication.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T05:02:01-07:00","id":115794,"title":"","content":"I think the gifts have a great theme going so far, some really have the feeling of being horror-esque, except this time You are the horror.<br /> Also really liking that with wisdom you can essentially possess anything, possession has an awesome amount of utility, really looking forwards to that!<br /> Its great news that the renown and gift system has been reworked, it definitely seems a lot smoother now, but I'll have to wait and see <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> ...Awwh I have to wait... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2044-fiere","name":"Fiere","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T05:15:14-07:00","id":115798,"title":"","content":"Not too happy with Gifts, but this is a symptom of my dislike of the Storytelling system; besides, the changes I was hoping to see would probably have been too fundamental for a 2nd edition of the game. So I can't really blame anyone for that.<br /> <br /> I kinda don't like the idea of all Shadow gifts being, at least in theory, equal in power. For all its flaws, I preferred the idea of 5-tiered powers.<br /> <br /> I love the level 5 Elodoth power, Ties of Blood and Bone, though. <i>Conceptually</i>, the individual powers are fantastic - I don't like the <i>structure</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T05:32:23-07:00","id":115803,"title":"","content":"Will I like what I see of the gifts themselves I'm still wondering whether or not it will make werewolves as much of an XP sink as before. I like that it's already reduced somewhat by not having an out of order XP hike anymore but that was just the tip of the iceberg. I guess we won't know until we see actual numbers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T05:33:44-07:00","id":115805,"title":"","content":"I think it's a different take on a way to re-do them though I think I'll need to see the full list when the book's out to form my final opinion. It's different but I do like that the Shadow Gifts especially possess a solid degree of utility from what I've seen. I had wondered if gifts were going to be on a system like this or more like Aspects and in a way, it seems they're both. As you buy up your Auspice renown you'll automatically gain a new ability in how you hunt.<br /> <br /> All in all? I'm excited and curious to see the total end result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1385-nickpire84","name":"Nickpire84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1385_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T06:47:20-07:00","id":115820,"title":"","content":"I notice there was no mention of Tribe Gifts. Do we still have those, and if so, do they work like Moon Gifts?<br /> <br /> With the new refocusing of Tribes onto a favored prey, it would make sense for each tribe to have a unique Gift to help them against that prey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T06:59:53-07:00","id":115824,"title":"","content":"I'd love to answer but for NDA reasons that's probably Stew's bailiwick. You're more likely to catch his notice and get a response if you post the question over on his Idigam Open Development blog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T07:23:25-07:00","id":115837,"title":"","content":"I like the Shadow/Wolf Gift structure. I\u2019m not so fond of the Moon Gift structure. I\u2019m especially looking forward to the Wolf Gifts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T07:25:05-07:00","id":115840,"title":"","content":"Looks pretty different from previous stuff. Will remain to see if I go with this new system or stick with the old one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T07:36:49-07:00","id":115846,"title":"","content":"I just love the slasher movie parallels with Gifts. They literally force a werewolf's target into acting out tropes that make the killer's job easier, like splitting away from the group or getting lost inside the den.<br /> <br /> Hunter: Hey guys, we stick together, right? Jessie Hell's a bit shy, we can at least make her afraid to attack.<br /> <br /> Jessie Hell: Suuure you will. *Divide And Conquer*<br /> <br /> Hunter: *fails roll* DUUUR, BUT I'M GETTING IMPATIENT PICK A DIRECTION AND START WALKING DAAAR...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T07:41:35-07:00","id":115848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daydreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=115820#post115820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I notice there was no mention of Tribe Gifts. Do we still have those, and if so, do they work like Moon Gifts? With the new refocusing of Tribes onto a favored prey, it would make sense for each tribe to have a unique Gift to help them against that prey.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well according to the blog, you start out with two Shadow Gifts determined by your Auspice and Tribe. So I would assume the Tribal Gifts will just be Tribe-specific Shadow Gifts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T07:44:09-07:00","id":115849,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I am a bit disappointed.<br /> <br /> My concern is it seems that while many of the low points from before were raised, many of the high points were lowered by the fact that many gifts now fall under a 3 dot power equivalent while we lose many 5 dots. While I am thrilled that the whole gift structure is being overhauled, the fact that there is a significant net reduction in higher end powers is a definite downside. In addition, they gifts themselves seem a bit bland especially when compared to Blood &amp; Smoke which I think did a fantastic job with power rewrites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T07:55:07-07:00","id":115857,"title":"","content":"Now, if these Shadow gift only costed 1xp...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T08:04:01-07:00","id":115867,"title":"","content":"Color me unenthused.<br /> <br /> Well, no, that's not entirely fair. These are generally much better than the old Gifts. That said, two points/concerns:<br /> <br /> 1) I'm saddened that we are still stuck with Renown, which seems like an unnecessary layer of complexity and an artificial speed bump in character development.<br /> 2) The fact that the first gift I see is &quot;perfect, unstoppable lie-detection&quot; makes me weep. So basically... social shenanigans do not work if there's an Elodoth in the party. Lovely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T08:04:08-07:00","id":115868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=115849#post115849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I am a bit disappointed.<br /> <br /> My concern is it seems that while many of the low points from before were raised, many of the high points were lowered by the fact that many gifts now fall under a 3 dot power equivalent while we lose many 5 dots. While I am thrilled that the whole gift structure is being overhauled, the fact that there is a significant net reduction in higher end powers is a definite downside. In addition, they gifts themselves seem a bit bland especially when compared to Blood &amp; Smoke which I think did a fantastic job with power rewrites.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see what you mean, when compared to Demon or Vampire the powers don't have the same feel of having a theme. In Demon all the powers simply had the feeling of the butterfly effect, one small change changes everything. In vampire everything felt Dark and destructive. These gifts, while some have a horror vibe, just feel like the werewolves are just doing something but don't have a similar spark.<br /> Another thing I would be interested to see is how one of these Werewolves fare against a higher vampire since we may hunt them. But the thing is that I feel they may be far more powerful, not only were their abilities strong, they also have more access to four and five dot abilities. Ah well, I guess I shall wait and see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2044-fiere","name":"Fiere","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T08:22:49-07:00","id":115876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fiere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=115868#post115868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see what you mean, when compared to Demon or Vampire the powers <b>don't have the same feel of having a theme</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I see one.<br /> <br /> All these werewolf powers have &quot;unstoppable hunter&quot; as a theme - removing advantages, forcing prey to behave stupidly, turning the environment to the Urathra's advantage - they force you to play by their rules, and in a fight with a shapeshifter on their level? Bet on the lycanthrope, every time.<br /> <br /> I do think the drafts need a little errata though, but I saw the &quot;first drafts&quot; label in the link. I have no doubt that starting from this area of awesome will help trim them up for prime time.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T08:27:07-07:00","id":115878,"title":"","content":"I love it! The relationship between Renown and Gifts kind of reminds me of Keys and Manifestations in Geist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T08:32:02-07:00","id":115883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=115876#post115876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All these werewolf powers have &quot;unstoppable hunter&quot; as a theme - removing advantages, forcing prey to behave stupidly, turning the environment to the Urathra's advantage - they force you to play by their rules, and in a fight with a shapeshifter on their level? Bet on the lycanthrope, every time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats true, I suppose the part I am unsure of is more related to the fluff. As in in Demon it felt that their powers were derived from nudging the fabric of fate, while in Vampire it felt like power was 'channeled' from the beast. It'd be awesome to see Werewolf gifts have the feeling of being spirit related.<br /> Anyway, I adore the new structure, the shadow gifts especially look awesome I'm in love with what you've done to them. Please keep up the good work! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2044-fiere","name":"Fiere","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T09:07:48-07:00","id":115908,"title":"","content":"Wisdom loves itself some Borrowing and I love it.<br /> I'm calling Pack Kin the &quot;Recruit Bears&quot; Facet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T09:20:50-07:00","id":115915,"title":"","content":"Your point of view of Renown is mine too. It's a complexity not necessary. The Aspects of the gifts could be tied directly to the Auspices in the new system. With perhaps a cost upgrade in Xp for those that are not tied to your auspice.<br /> <br /> Neither my players nor mine like the Renown has it is actually.<br /> <br /> For the gifts system, yes, it seem much better.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2307-arcanum-magicae","name":"Arcanum Magicae","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T09:24:13-07:00","id":115917,"title":"","content":"I think you lot are being overly harsh in a few ways. I like that it's been simplified as it has been. I've always wanted a gift list similar to vampire, where what you can have is based on what your character SHOULD have. Not &quot;here's a grab bag of special magics go to town! BUT YOU CAN ONLY HAVE 3!!&quot; This adds a structure to the game that it needed. <br /> <br /> The elodoth abilities look amazing for people who will be playing that (my fiance will love it), and Irraka looks exactly like something my brother would want. Nature gifts? Hell yes. Technology gifts? Deconstruct? Uratha are monsterously dangerous now. A good chunk of you might see something bland, or unimpressive but I see new ways to play beyond &quot;the wolf must smash.&quot; <br /> <br /> Remember it's all around a hunting theme. We can have proper wolf packs performing proper hunts, no longer just an extended action but and actual. Proper. Hunt. I'm friggin excited!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T09:33:24-07:00","id":115921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=115917#post115917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember it's all around a hunting theme. We can have proper wolf packs performing proper hunts, no longer just an extended action but and actual. Proper. Hunt. I'm friggin excited!!</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems that any 'we need to get shit done' is being turned thematically into a hunt. And I am super ok with that.<br /> <br /> And havving thought about it - I think I might be digging Renown more now on a metaphysical basis. It's a representation of the Human side of a werewolf, that which is exalted and identified with beyond the instinctual. A wolf doesn't give a shit about another wolf's wisdowm or glory or whatever, but a human does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T09:53:24-07:00","id":115926,"title":"","content":"I think it's cool how some of the gifts allow you to add your Renown to dice pools. That should help give Uratha an additional nasty advantage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T09:53:36-07:00","id":115927,"title":"","content":"A bit sad, really, that truth powers are restricted to one auspice. Scenting lies is a big thing with werewolf stories. Ah, well. Overall, sounds like an update of the All .good Gifts hack in the chronicler's guide. Auto-gain auspice stuff as you level renown, then earn Gifts as normal. Some twisting of words. We effectively have Wisdom, Purity, etc as the Gift categories now. Nothing too shocking or unexpected to warrant the excitement, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T10:05:37-07:00","id":115931,"title":"","content":"AWESOME. Cool and thematic powers, a very big improvement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T10:16:19-07:00","id":115936,"title":"","content":"I'm seriously amped about this new take on gifts! They all seem brutally useful, which seems like the kind of thing werewolves would like in their powers. I also love the enforcement of Renown's importance both mechanically and within the fluff, it helps to simplify the potential of these powers and add some oomph to the various aspects of a werewolf's nature (they're becoming the Wolf version of Mummy's Pillars, and I'm super OK with that).<br /> <br /> All in all, I'm actually excited to play Werewolf: the Forsaken again!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/671-the-lone-gunman","name":"The Lone Gunman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T10:48:36-07:00","id":115945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=115917#post115917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you lot are being overly harsh in a few ways. I like that it's been simplified as it has been. I've always wanted a gift list similar to vampire, where what you can have is based on what your character SHOULD have. Not &quot;here's a grab bag of special magics go to town! BUT YOU CAN ONLY HAVE 3!!&quot; This adds a structure to the game that it needed.<br /> <br /> The elodoth abilities look amazing for people who will be playing that (my fiance will love it), and Irraka looks exactly like something my brother would want. Nature gifts? Hell yes. Technology gifts? Deconstruct? Uratha are monsterously dangerous now. A good chunk of you might see something bland, or unimpressive but I see new ways to play beyond &quot;the wolf must smash.&quot;<br /> <br /> Remember it's all around a hunting theme. We can have proper wolf packs performing proper hunts, no longer just an extended action but and actual. Proper. Hunt. I'm friggin excited!!</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, the new Gifts are awesome! I love the thematic vibe each of the Gifts in the draft have especially since Stew has been emphasizing 'The Wolf Must Hunt', and the Gifts totally line up with that. While I was initially hesitant and skeptical as I was reading through Stew's post, reading through the draft completely changed my opinion. I like that Moon Gifts are still tiered, while Shadow Gifts have different Facets that are each equivalent to one another. It's a very different take compared to all the other game lines' powers and something unique. Despite concerns people may have with whether these three-dot Shadow Gifts could keep up with other splats, I have no doubt that they most definitely can. The sample Shadow Gifts are all quite useful and flexible, allowing you a variety of options. Knotted Paths allows you to trap your prey within a certain vicinity, causing them to wind up back where they started. Pack Kin is especially awesome, so since you can now bring in mammals into your pack! I also love the fact that Uratha can become Claimed if they lose their bodies while using Beast Ride or Iron Slave. There is so much potential and versatility with each of these Gifts, I just love it! Keep up the good work Stew and company, it's been fantastic so far!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1198-devil-bunny","name":"devil bunny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T10:56:41-07:00","id":115953,"title":"","content":"Is it me or are Werewolves the new Slashers?<br /> <br /> That said, as much as I like the definite improvement in the increase in power, I miss being a shaman. I suppose if we can still control or bind spirits we'll see it in the rituals spoiler.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T11:02:57-07:00","id":115959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=115953#post115953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it me or are Werewolves the new Slashers?<br /> <br /> That said, as much as I like the definite improvement in the increase in power, I miss being a shaman. I suppose if we can still control or bind spirits we'll see it in the rituals spoiler.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why miss? The shaman aspect was increasingly linked with Rites and not with gifts. A part that is (unfortunately) often forget.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1999-wolf","name":"Wolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1999_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T11:16:13-07:00","id":115970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=115953#post115953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it me or are Werewolves the new Slashers? That said, as much as I like the definite improvement in the increase in power, I miss being a shaman. I suppose if we can still control or bind spirits we'll see it in the rituals spoiler.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm sure rituals will pick up that slack. And I wouldn't be surprised if there are shaman-y Gifts as well. Crescent moon sounded awesome, starting out letting you see spirits and capping off letting you sense any spirit in a very wide radius and see through any of their senses. I assume that won't be the only Gift that focuses on interacting with spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T11:57:21-07:00","id":116008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=115953#post115953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it me or are Werewolves the new Slashers?</div> </div> </div> </div>As it should be. Or at least a compliment to Slashers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T12:21:35-07:00","id":116024,"title":"","content":"&quot;They may see a desirable object like juicy fruit-&quot;-What, the gum? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Okay, soooooo Gifts. Let's attack this two ways: The Structure and the Gifts themselves.<br /> <br /> 1)The Structure.<br /> <br /> Let me get two things on the table immediately.<br /> <br /> a)I like the new setup...<br /> b)..even if it somewhat concerns me about EXP.<br /> <br /> Someone made the comparison to Geist's Keys and Manifestations(reversed, this is like scale-able keys and locked manifestations, and that's actually a lot of what I felt with it. This is a good thing in my opinion as quite frankly I loved the way the plug and play feel of that mechanic. Whatever I might say later in this post about it, Renown makes the most sense as the root of this entire program, with Gifts and their Facets being unlocked by that. Whether it be that you're rewarded with Moon Gifts by becoming better at what you inherently do or just getting the spirits to respond to you as a person, a lot of this feel very natural, with some catches. It also feels more like, well, Gifts, powers granted in respect to a werewolf's spiritual growth, where before there was a greater emphasis on the bargaining side of things. It's just really superb, it feels immensely streamlined and clear from the word go what I'm supposed to do.<br /> <br /> But I mentioned catches.<br /> <br /> First off, unlike Keys and Manifestations, you can't just plug and play, despite what I said. Raising your Auspice Renown means you get a Moon Facet and a new Shadow Gift, assumedly with the facet in what you just increased, but raising other Renown grant Facets from Gifts you already have-so you need to buy Gifts in order to have something to plug into. We're still somewhat in that Geist-esque realm, but then account that if you want a Facet without raising Renown, you have to buy that separately. I <i>think</i> that's how it goes, I might be wrong. But the point is that it's a far cry from &quot;Buy key, can plug into whichever Manifestation&quot;-there's some extra paperwork involved. I'm not saying Werewolf has to be Geist, far from it, but when the parallels exist, the flaws of one stand out in contrast to the others.<br /> <br /> A lot of this will come down to the expense of Gifts, Facets, and <i>especiall</i><i>y</i> Renown. If the price is right, this is a minor issue, but if it's not, then we have taken a two way EXP sink and turned it into a three way, little-bit-confusing-and-yet-somehow-more-streamlined EXP sink.<br /> <br /> I don't say that as a naysayer-On the whole I am really optimistic and happy with the new Gift Structure instituted here. I have to acknowledge what seems like flaws, but the way it works out is really, really cool to me.<br /> <br /> And then there are the Gifts themselves...<br /> <br /> 2)The Gifts<br /> <br /> There have been a lot of &quot;Werewolves are the new Slashers&quot; comments. And you know what, they're right! Well, almost. Slashers emphasize just straight up killing you. Be unseen in someway and then take you out, regardless of what advantages you might have. Werewolves are close, but not quite there, and they actually hit on slasher tropes a lot more, as noted(In that sense, it's absolutely right, going by genre and not template). I'm fascinated by how werewolves strip options away from their target, not only for the slasher metaphor but also because it makes things more feral. Gifts seems really about reducing everything down to caveman days in some form or fashion, and leaving it truly predator versus prey. It's viscerally frightening, in the same way the Disciplines from Blood and Smoke got really scary really quick, and I like that. I feel hunted reading these, and <i>I</i> <i>like it</i>.<br /> <br /> Digging more in the individual concepts, I love how evocative the Auspice gifts are. The Elodoth really feel like mediators and social hunters, cutting through the bullshit and binding people with their own extensive web of people, and the Irraka are the reason we're talking about Slashers, let's be honest. Eviscerate in particular was brutal to read, like the Devs just said &quot;No, forget going slow and making it easier for you to hide and get your prey, no, let's just straight up give you the reason you want to do those things in the first place, and then make it easier&quot;. That's a good thing! It has immediate appeal! And from there they just become like a killing mist-you can't really stop it, it just slips in everywhere and eats you as you curl up in a corner crying for your doggy. It's like B&amp;S's Nosferatu, but skipping the bullshit and getting to the point(which is grossly missing the idea, I admit-the Nossies fear mongering <i>is</i> the point, where being the assassin is the point for Irraka).<br /> <br /> Nature weird me out a little, given how much city is in it, but that aside I like the synergy of it all, particularly between Nature Cunning, Honor, and Glory's facets. Also, to everyone wondering if wolves can be part of the pack, Nature Purity just answered with a hearty &quot;Yes&quot;, and I'm glad it's likely the Rahu who will do that.<br /> <br /> Technology felt much like a repeating track to me, with all of them being shades of &quot;Take Out Your Tools&quot;-but that said, beyond a basic use of each in that consistent theme, each does fill roles and uses beyond and aside, and encourages(you guessed it) pack cooperation and synergy, which is kind of cool. I don't have much to say about them.<br /> <br /> A final thing is on the Elodoth's gifts, and this is a 'just me' thing-There was always this vague sense of Elodoth and Cahalith commonly serving as pack pa's and ma's respectively in the old edition-nothing heavy, just minorly there. I bring this up because the Elodoth have the ability to swap with pack mates at their highest renown, but not to know what state they are in. So if Cahalith retain the ability to know where people are and what they're doing(And I hope they do, I liked that particular trick a lot), that kinda continues the vague trend, and that amuses me. It's just a cool thing.<br /> <br /> On the whole I had a very positive take away from this. I like how predatory the gifts themselves feel, and I like natural progression and growth of the gift structure. Gifts have an identity now, rather than just being a cluster of things, and that's the one thing it needed more than anything else in comparison to just about every other game-Gifts <i>feel </i>like Werewolf now.<br /> <br /> PS: My laptop's wireless driver is so dead, Dessie. You could have won this week no problem. Instead, Bunyip gets the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-19-2014, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T12:57:39-07:00","id":116051,"title":"","content":"Overall pleased with the new Gift system itself.<br /> <br /> Haven't seen any straight +2's or +1's to (situation) that were all over the place in Forsaken originally. Closet thing are scaling buffs, which is fine and even interesting as long as the situations aren't too specific. That's good. The general level of power and utility in the Gifts is refreshing as well, unlike in Forsaken where you really have to cherry pick in this I see many a power that I'd happily consider dumping exp to get.<br /> <br /> Splitting the gifts themselves into categories that behave differently is an interesting move. I like the work-around to dealing with Renown being part of the activation pool by making Moon gifts tiered and always one renown, but then having Shadow gifts be partitioned based on what kind of renown it uses. It does make me wonder if there should be some bonus you get if you take all 5 fragments of a specific Shadow gift, I think that'd be nifty on several levels. Do wish we had seen some examples of Wolf gifts though, they're pretty ambiguous at the moment.<br /> <br /> Still somewhat worried about two things that have plagued Forsaken since it came out though: Specificity and Renown cost.<br /> <br /> When I say specificity I'm referring to the general habit of Forsaken powers to have a &quot;This, but not this&quot; setup. <br /> Scent of Taint was a great example in that it let you smell the taint of the unnatural on someone else's scent, but only on someone's scent and not something's scent (so you could smell that there was something up with a Ghoul for instance, but a magical artifact of untold power wouldn't register) and it specifically wouldn't give you a heads up as to what kind of supernatural power it was even with context clues like (smells of blood/ozone/fruit). Also it doesn't work on ephemeral beings like spirits and ghosts unless they're possessing a body. Still worth taking in theory, but weirdly hampered by it's own &quot;but&quot; clause. <br /> <br /> Another example is... the issue of Twilight. I've run crossover games before and if there's one thing that's frustrating it's how limited werewolves tend to be when it comes to stuff in Twilight, but how incredibly good other splats tend to have it through a single utility power. For instance werewolves don't have a natural See in Twilight power, they have a built-in ability that lets them see glimmers of spirits if they're in Twilight; if it's a ghost though, you need a Death gift to see it. If it's not a Ghost or a Spirit and it's in Twilight...well tough cookies, you can't see it. Want to actually touch it? Well if it's a spirit there's a 2 dot ritual for that (and maybe klaives? I can't remember if there's a rule for it, but I run with Klaives having spirit-touch automatically). If it's a ghost there's a Death Gift for that. If it's neither, there's a very specific fetish that effects all Twilight things so hopefully someone in your pack has that. Sounds reasonable, then the Ulgan (it was a weird chronicle) spends a pyros and can see/touch all things in Twilight for a scene regardless of what it is. This sort of lopsided tendency of giving werewolves several powers that collectively amount to a single power another template gets is disappointingly common and while I'm not trying to make a Template X is Better than Template Y Because Z argument, the amount of clutter built directly into Forsaken needs to be addressed.<br /> <br /> Renown cost is another issue I'm weary about. Hopefully there's a new system on how to get Renown, either through Renown having its own little subsystem or just straight up virtual exp (You did a glorious thing! +1 Glory exp! etc.). Either one will be a fantastic addition to the game and will avoid a situation that's somewhat intolerable as a player. It's happened to me before in chronicles where I just didn't have the infinite exp required to get the renown for stuff that I did in fact do.<br /> <br /> So I'm running around with Wisdom 3 and Cunning 2, but through my deeds should have Purity 1, Honor 1, Glory 3, Wisdom 4, and Cunning 3. It was an eventful chronicle and I managed to do a lot of nifty stuff, which was cool, as soon as I had enough exp I could start getting more Renown...but there wasn't really an in-character reason for this tremendous lag in Doing the Deed and Getting the Renown. Like after I got the killing blow on the mysterious abomination that had just killed our alpha and took a trophy from its corpse, by all measures I should have undergone the Rite of the Spirit Brand to mark the occasion. Instead I had to put it off for about a year so I could get the experience to afford it. When asked about it in-character the only response I could give is &quot;Uhhhh...I just haven't gotten around to it. #shrug&quot;<br /> <br /> Hopefully <b>that</b> is gone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T13:07:02-07:00","id":116055,"title":"","content":"I'm concerned with how this system will work with character development, personally. By having the bulk of available Gifts be 3-dot equivalents of different applications, I foresee two related results: Werewolves are going to be really powerful out-of-the-gate, with starting characters able to pull some really nasty tricks; but also once they start gaining exp they're going to have roughly the same power-level, only diversified across a wider range of applications. [Moon Gifts are clearly an exception, but the majority of abilities are Shadow Gifts.] This system doesn't look like it works well for specialization or progression..... As a player and storyteller who prefers long-running chronicles (and also crossover opportunities), I'm skeptical.<br /> <br /> <br /> [Edit/addition:] I don't mean to sound strictly like a critic. As far as the feel, theme, and capability of the new Gifts, I'm really rather excited. Like a lot of other people here, I read them and cooed &quot;awesome...&quot; and they all contribute well to the Wolf Must Hunt theme, the emphasis of which is something I'm most looking forward to in <i>Idigam</i>. But, I have concerns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 04-19-2014, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T13:08:18-07:00","id":116056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, to everyone wondering if wolves can be part of the pack, Nature Purity just answered with a hearty &quot;Yes&quot;, and I'm glad it's likely the Rahu who will do that. </div> </div> </div>Even better, it's not just wolves--it can be ANY predatory animal. Bear, mountain lion, hawk, you name it. If it hunts other animals, it's fair game. A house cat could be a very useful friend, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T13:18:18-07:00","id":116059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116055#post116055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm concerned with how this system will work with character development, personally. By having the bulk of available Gifts be 3-dot equivalents of different applications, I foresee two related results: Werewolves are going to be really powerful out-of-the-gate, with starting characters able to pull some really nasty tricks; but also once they start gaining exp they're going to have roughly the same power-level, only diversified across a wider range of applications. [Moon Gifts are clearly an exception, but the majority of abilities are Shadow Gifts.] This system doesn't look like it works well for specialization or progression..... As a player and storyteller who prefers long-running chronicles (and also crossover opportunities), I'm skeptical.</div> </div> </div> </div> I would be more concerned if Gifts were the only powers Werewolves could get. But in addition to Moon Gifts you've got Rituals and Werewolf-Specific merits for vertical growth, and who knows, we may even get more than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T13:30:40-07:00","id":116067,"title":"","content":"Bring other predatory animals into the pack? Hohoho, I see possibilities. For example, birds of prey as sentries. Or a pack that lives on a boat. Would you like to have half a dozen huge sharks at your beck and call? (or if you want to go really wild, orcas). <br /> <br /> A question about Unmake. What is the upper limit for this Gift? It mentions cars as possible targets. Does that mean that main battle tanks are also susceptible? Just how big a target can you affect? What happens if you use it on an aircraft carrier?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1631-karthak","name":"Karthak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1631_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T13:34:59-07:00","id":116069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116059#post116059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I would be more concerned if Gifts were the only powers Werewolves could get. But in addition to Moon Gifts you've got Rituals and Werewolf-Specific merits for vertical growth, and who knows, we may even get more than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, and we'll see how that goes. I'm skeptical, not set against it; I&quot;m waiting and hoping my concerns will be smoothed over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T13:45:55-07:00","id":116074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karthak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116067#post116067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bring other predatory animals into the pack? Hohoho, I see possibilities. For example, birds of prey as sentries. Or a pack that lives on a boat. Would you like to have half a dozen huge sharks at your beck and call? (or if you want to go really wild, orcas).<br /> <br /> A question about Unmake. What is the upper limit for this Gift? It mentions cars as possible targets. Does that mean that main battle tanks are also susceptible? Just how big a target can you affect? What happens if you use it on an aircraft carrier?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Werewolves at war are a particularly nasty idea now. At land or at sea.<br /> <br /> I said they were a lot like slashers before, and I really am digging that. Even if you aren't going to play werewolf, they suddenly make for scary antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T14:18:35-07:00","id":116099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116059#post116059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I would be more concerned if Gifts were the only powers Werewolves could get. But in addition to Moon Gifts you've got Rituals and Werewolf-Specific merits for vertical growth, and who knows, we may even get more than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking about merits, I want to see some new Uratha Fighting Styles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T14:29:00-07:00","id":116111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116074#post116074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Werewolves at war are a particularly nasty idea now. At land or at sea.<br /> <br /> I said they were a lot like slashers before, and I really am digging that. Even if you aren't going to play werewolf, they suddenly make for scary antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh shit.<br /> <br /> You would need an amazing amount of successes for it, but I'm imagining an F-15 flying at an Uratha only to fucking fall apart past them.<br /> <br /> Others can do that, sure, and can even control probability to not get hit, but none of them can pull off the badass look of a near-man werewolf snarling the damn thing down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T14:52:13-07:00","id":116128,"title":"","content":"I'm very much liking what I see here. I expected Renown to shift to what we see in Pendragon's Gifts system, and am surprised by how different it really is. I also love the gifts draft, we do lose some potentially powerful gifts because all new Shadow/Wolf gifts are 'equal to rank 3' but I'm loving that these Gifts lets Uratha from any auspice or renown buy into them to get what they want, and expect the Auspice/Tribe=&gt;Gifts list to be pretty open ended. As well if you want those powerful 5 dotters, buy Auspice gifts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I know a lot of folks dislike Renown, but I personally think it's one of the integral parts of Werewolf. That werewolves are marked not by age or raw skill, but by achievement. With the new XP system it won't be remotely as huge an XP dump to get some of the (previously) high ranking Gifts. Bravo! Love the new system, cannot wait to explore it with my players. Particularly enjoy that each Gift has an aspect of the hunt in it. Each gift gives an advantage to the hunters over their prey. It really does reinforce the idiom 'The Wolf Must Hunt.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1824,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","user":"Xaielao","date":". 04-19-2014, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","name":"Xaielao","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T14:56:18-07:00","id":116130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116111#post116111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh shit.<br /> <br /> You would need an amazing amount of successes for it, but I'm imagining an F-15 flying at an Uratha only to fucking fall apart past them.<br /> <br /> Others can do that, sure, and can even control probability to not get hit, but none of them can pull off the badass look of a near-man werewolf snarling the damn thing down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or instead that Uratha takes control of the F-15 and flies it at the attackers with Iron Slave! OMG the potential for the new Gifts, I'm loving that there are so many ways they could be used, especially when compared to the core W:tF gifts, half of which seemed to only be useful on a rare occasion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1824,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","user":"Xaielao","date":". 04-19-2014, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","name":"Xaielao","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T15:21:56-07:00","id":116151,"title":"","content":"It might just be word choice, but when they call individual powers Fragments I can't help but think you might get something nifty if you put all of them together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T15:37:43-07:00","id":116163,"title":"","content":"All in all, the new gift system does look like an improvement over the previous one. If for no other reason the its narrowing down the number of gift categories and simplifying character progression in this particular area. <br /> <br /> Still I do have issues that are basically summed up by this poster:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NeoTiamat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=115867#post115867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Color me unenthused.<br /> <br /> Well, no, that's not entirely fair. These are generally much better than the old Gifts. That said, two points/concerns:<br /> <br /> 1) I'm saddened that we are still stuck with Renown, which seems like an unnecessary layer of complexity and an artificial speed bump in character development.<br /> 2) The fact that the first gift I see is &quot;perfect, unstoppable lie-detection&quot; makes me weep. So basically... social shenanigans do not work if there's an Elodoth in the party. Lovely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Renown was always something I was very dubious of in the previous incarnation of the game. Mainly because I felt the renown system was a little fast and loose and could be abused a little. However, I acknowledge that without knowing how the developers have likely revamped and changed the Renown system this is at current perhaps an unfair criticism to throw at Gifts. <br /> <br /> Yeah, I loath perfect lie-detection powers. Universally take a load of intrigue and plot off the table, second only to certain &quot;sight&quot; powers for sheer annoyance as an ST. Auspex in Blood and Smoke can fall into similar territory but at least its using up vitae after the first use, taxing a person. The Eloodoth power is what 1 Essence for a scene...yeah. <br /> <br /> (As a side note one of the things about Demon that made me happy was the section expressly saying truth/lie detecting powers just flat-out don't work on Demons, even if they are involved more with fate then the truth or falseness of the statement the Demon makes. So that at least keeps Demon cross-over viable, good luck crossing over the other major intrigue game line (Vampire) with this though.) <br /> <br /> The other issue I have was raised by the following poster:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fiere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=115867#post115867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see what you mean, when compared to Demon or Vampire the powers don't have the same feel of having a theme. In Demon all the powers simply had the feeling of the butterfly effect, one small change changes everything. In vampire everything felt Dark and destructive. These gifts, while some have a horror vibe, just feel like the werewolves are just doing something but don't have a similar spark.</div> </div> </div> </div>As posters since have pointed out there is a very general theme of &quot;hunting&quot; in the gifts, but its spread really thin I feel. <br /> <br /> Every single Discipline in Blood and Smoke felt like it was getting across the theme of either &quot;letting a bit of the beast out into the world&quot; or &quot;being inherently destructive/negative/degrading in nature&quot;. Demon did not do quite so good a job with its Embeds and Exploits, some powers obviously being added it because &quot;they are totally spies!&quot; or &quot;yeah demons = fire get it&quot;. However, it still did a really good job of the underpinned idea of &quot;hacking reality&quot;. <br /> <br /> Things like amazing ambush attacks or bending other predatory creatures to your will I can dig and very &quot;Werewolf&quot; in feel. Making an object break/disassemble or causing all the lights to short-circuit not so much. I really in two minds about the whole &quot;riding other things sense&quot; powers as well. I can kinda see it (at least the animal one, the machine one gave me another case of WTF) but I think I would have preferred those more &quot;obvious&quot; magical powers be Rites. <br /> <br /> \u200bBasically, its mechanically a vast improvement for the most part, I'm still unsure about the sorta breath and type of powers that are included in Gifts. Plus keeping their link to the Renown mechanic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T15:44:57-07:00","id":116174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Red 9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116151#post116151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might just be word choice, but when they call individual powers Fragments I can't help but think you might get something nifty if you put all of them together.</div> </div> </div> </div>They call them Facets. Mean this is how one would look at this Gift from the view of Cunning/Honor/etc. However, your idea does give me cause to think. Like that might be a neat way to go for Milestone Gifts. Like someone gaining all of the Technology Gifts goes on to learn the Final Gift of Technology. Perhaps powering up the previously learned gifts, or being its own power.<br /> <br /> Hmmm, probably something for later books. But definitely adds an idea for Elder stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T16:19:29-07:00","id":116199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116174#post116174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They call them Facets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do they?<br /> <br /> They do. I'm dumb. Still I like the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T16:30:44-07:00","id":116206,"title":"","content":"So do I! It rings of a certain style I can follow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T16:49:39-07:00","id":116210,"title":"","content":"If my players get all the facets of a gift, I'm making them a milestone to cap it off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T17:12:26-07:00","id":116222,"title":"","content":"So just to Clarify:<ul><li>A werewolf character starts out with one Moon Gift determined by her Auspice, two Shadow Gifts chosen from a list determined by her Tribe, and the two Wolf Gifts.</li> <li>Whenever a character earns a dot of Renown, she gets a free Facet in one of the Shadow or Wolf Gifts she already knows.</li> <li>Whenever a character earns a dot of her Auspice\u2019s favored Renown, she gets the next dot in her Moon Gift <i>and </i>a new Shadow Gift.</li> <li>Additional Shadow Gifts and Facets can be bought with Experiences</li> </ul>Assuming this is all correct and I didn\u2019t misunderstand something, the questions I am left with are:<ul><li>Does the free Facet you get from buying a Renown dot have to be associated with that type of Renown, or can you buy a dot of Glory and get a Purity Facet?</li> <li>Do you still get a free Facet in one of your Shadow Gifts when you buy a dot in your Auspice Renown?</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T17:54:50-07:00","id":116243,"title":"","content":"I like the Scent Beneath the Surface gift. I've been running vampire, and before that playing changeling for a long time and I gotta say it wouldn't end social dilemmas as much as people are making it out.<br /> <br /> For one, it's not exactly a lie detector as much as a deceit detector. With most lie detectors, you can just easily avoid any magical abilities by using lies of omission, and this ability does scent those out.<br /> Two, it doesn't give you any more than a 'They are being deceitful,' gauge. Granted, if you had planned on a character who told really convincing lies and was never detected, you may have a problem, but one can take for granted that a monster like a vampire or a mage is going to lie to you (or keep things from you), and an alert at their comments doesn't really mean that now whatever they planned doesn't work. 'Did you tell anyone about our plan?' 'No.' a whiff of deceit on that can mean anything from, 'I told my wife but it doesn't matter, she doesn't believe in this stuff anyways,' to 'I told every hunter in the city and they're waiting for you.'<br /> Three, the result is (as it should be) up to the players. Some might decide to use other abilities (Intimidate, Brawl) right off the bat, others may decide to just keep their guard up afterward. The idea that it dead-ends plots is ridiculous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T18:46:25-07:00","id":116267,"title":"","content":"With Scent Beneath the Surface, I would assume that in a later form of it, a supernatural template would probably have a clash of wills or a contested roll of some kind especially if using a power to enhance his social abilities. Keep in mind, this is still a first draft","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T19:18:01-07:00","id":116283,"title":"","content":"I'd like to take a moment to call into question the reading comprehension of everyone complaining about &quot;perfect lie detection,&quot; because <i>that is not what a contested roll means.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T22:17:14-07:00","id":116336,"title":"","content":"I seem a bit confused. According to the description of Death Gifts it says that both the Rahu and Irakka would gain the wisdom facet of Death's Gift. How does this work? I thought you chose the Gift that gained a Renown's facet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T22:34:41-07:00","id":116342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116336#post116336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seem a bit confused. According to the description of Death Gifts it says that both the Rahu and Irakka would gain the wisdom facet of Death's Gift. How does this work? I thought you chose the Gift that gained a Renown's facet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that the lead-in mentions that you start with two Shadow Gifts chosen based on your tribe and auspice and the example itself leads with both of the characters having the Gift of Death, I don't think it's too much of a stretch to guess that starting Renown will still have the basic elements of &quot;at least one dot each in tribal and auspice Renown&quot; and that this will affect your starting Shadow Gifts' Facets accordingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T23:17:05-07:00","id":116356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116222#post116222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>Does the free Facet you get from buying a Renown dot have to be associated with that type of Renown, or can you buy a dot of Glory and get a Purity Facet?</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div> Conceptually, why would advancing in one type of Renown unlock something from another type? (I'm trying to understand the logic behind your question.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T23:31:23-07:00","id":116359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116356#post116356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Conceptually, why would advancing in one type of Renown unlock something from another type? (I'm trying to understand the logic behind your question.)</div> </div> </div> </div> Conceptually, I can't imagine why it would. That's why I asked, because from the blog entry, it doesn't sound like there's any mechanical reason you couldn't, but conceptually it doesn't seem like you should be able to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T02:09:13-07:00","id":116418,"title":"","content":"Please, PLEASE, explain me - will werewolves have powers wich equal to 5-dot Disciplines or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T02:26:48-07:00","id":116422,"title":"","content":"I have a few things I need to get off of my chest.<br /> <br /> First off. Awesome idea. The general idea of how Gifts are supposed to work now is something I love. It's just a bit unclear. Can you buy into Gifts not given by Tribe or Totem? Or are you stuck with those that you start with? And will Lodges grant more Gifts? Because Lodges having esoteric Gifts was one of the fun things.<br /> <br /> Secondly. The Shadow Gifts seem a bit... Weak. Not bad, but just a bit underpowered. They feel like they are on the level with Demon Embeds, but they all cost Essence. And several of them cost multiple Essence (Essences?). And none of them come even close to the higher level Disciplines. They are about two dot Disciplines. And the gifts doesn't at ALL close the gap that stuff like Vigor and Resilience put between Uratha and Kindred. But I hope (oh gods how I hope) that this gets handled by Werewolf shape shifting. A werewolf shouldn't have to be afraid to face a young vampire in one-on-one. At least it should be equal.<br /> The high level gifts were one of the few things that made Uratha terrifying monsters. Things like Savage Might, Thunderbolt, Vanish and Primal Form were pure terror. Sure, there were many bad 5 dot powers (Most, in fact.), but the solution to that should be fixing the bad ones, not remove them all, should it?<br /> <br /> Thirdly. Are the Wolf Gifts ONLY the old Father Wolf and Mother Luna gifts? Or do they involve things like Strength and Stealth as well? Since they don't really feel magical in the same way, they are just enhancements of the Uratha in question after all.<br /> <br /> Fourthly (Is that a word?), The wording for the Unmake Tech Gift is kinda weird. I don't know about you, but I'd classify an axe as something simple without moving parts. Should it have a -2 or -4 penalty? More examples are needed!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T03:22:44-07:00","id":116429,"title":"","content":"1) Yes.<br /> <br /> 2) The Wisdom Facet of the Technology Gift was a 4 dots; the next thing that could grant an Irraka Rote action to rolls before (granted, not exclusively to brawl and weaponry) was a 5 dots gift.<br /> <br /> 3) Yes, for now only the Changing and Hunting Gifts are the Wolf one.<br /> <br /> 4) -4 (Simple <b>and</b> no moving parts) Go with -2 and -2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T05:17:54-07:00","id":116449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116422#post116422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a few things I need to get off of my chest.<br /> <br /> First off. Awesome idea. The general idea of how Gifts are supposed to work now is something I love. It's just a bit unclear. Can you buy into Gifts not given by Tribe or Totem? Or are you stuck with those that you start with? And will Lodges grant more Gifts? Because Lodges having esoteric Gifts was one of the fun things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't comment on the Lodges part, but yes, you can buy into Gifts outside of your affinity picks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116422#post116422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly. The Shadow Gifts seem a bit... Weak. Not bad, but just a bit underpowered. They feel like they are on the level with Demon Embeds, but they all cost Essence. And several of them cost multiple Essence (Essences?). And none of them come even close to the higher level Disciplines. They are about two dot Disciplines. And the gifts doesn't at ALL close the gap that stuff like Vigor and Resilience put between Uratha and Kindred. But I hope (oh gods how I hope) that this gets handled by Werewolf shape shifting. A werewolf shouldn't have to be afraid to face a young vampire in one-on-one. At least it should be equal.</div> </div> </div> </div>With all due respect (honestly), you haven't seen the rest of the game/system yet. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> We haven't gotten to playtesting yet, but just going from the writer's bible, I'm not too worried overall about the hypothetical combat between a vampire and a werewolf. Of course, that still stands on what the context of the fight is - what's the situation, the area the fight is taking place in, why are they fighting, things like that. If you're talking a white-room scenario, then I can't really speak to that as, personally, I don't find those sorts of things terribly useful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116422#post116422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The high level gifts were one of the few things that made Uratha terrifying monsters. Things like Savage Might, Thunderbolt, Vanish and Primal Form were pure terror. Sure, there were many bad 5 dot powers (Most, in fact.), but the solution to that should be fixing the bad ones, not remove them all, should it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as someone who's played a character with Vanish...it wasn't quite all it was cracked up to be. By the mechanics, all Vanish really does is levy a -5 penalty on sight-based Perception rolls. Sure, if you get into combat, the opponents use the &quot;Fighting Blind&quot; rules, but I never really found the Gift (by RAW) to really feel like it lived up to what the description of the Gift was selling. Other 5-dot Gifts were much more powerful - although of course, any Gift can come in useful in the right circumstances.<br /> <br /> When we saw the Gifts draft, I took an old character of mine and re-did his Gifts based on his Renown. Not only did he end up having more Gifts/Facets due to the way Auspice Gifts work now, overall his Gifts had a tighter and more thematic focus. He lost some stuff, but gained new abilities that are far more evocative of a hunting wolf. And as the character is a Hunter in Darkness Elodoth, that very much fit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116422#post116422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thirdly. Are the Wolf Gifts ONLY the old Father Wolf and Mother Luna gifts? Or do they involve things like Strength and Stealth as well? Since they don't really feel magical in the same way, they are just enhancements of the Uratha in question after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hunting and Changing Gifts are pretty cool, but I'm afraid I can't speak particulars on them quite yet. Chris may be able to say more whenever he's back to his computer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116422#post116422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fourthly (Is that a word?), The wording for the Unmake Tech Gift is kinda weird. I don't know about you, but I'd classify an axe as something simple without moving parts. Should it have a -2 or -4 penalty? More examples are needed!</div> </div> </div> </div>If there is any lack of clarity, that's what redlines and playtesting are for - to find those and clear them up. Thanks for pointing it out!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T06:30:52-07:00","id":116472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116449#post116449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't comment on the Lodges part, but yes, you can buy into Gifts outside of your affinity picks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another thing that was kinda unclear. Does one have to buy the Gift as a whole, before one can start picking Facets from it, or can you just decide &quot;Nah, now I want the Cunning Facet of... Hmm. That list way, way over there.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, when you raise Renown, do you have to stay within Affinity?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116449#post116449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With all due respect (honestly), you haven't seen the rest of the game/system yet. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I know, I know. I was merely commenting on first looks. I think the Shadow Gifts we saw were a bit weak compared to the powers of Demons and Vampires, is mostly all. The Moon Gifts are awesome though, if a tad expensive at the end.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116449#post116449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We haven't gotten to playtesting yet, but just going from the writer's bible, I'm not too worried overall about the hypothetical combat between a vampire and a werewolf. Of course, that still stands on what the context of the fight is - what's the situation, the area the fight is taking place in, why are they fighting, things like that. If you're talking a white-room scenario, then I can't really speak to that as, personally, I don't find those sorts of things terribly useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, White Room fights are rarely useful, but it might be worth considering how much one has to stack a fight to make it come out in one's favour. The physical disciplines of the vampires are crazy strong. Which I like, I might add. I just want werewolves to be on par with that. While having to rely on one's pack for fights is extremely thematic, it isn't very fun to be forced into it. Cooperation should be a strength, not a requirement. At least in my opinion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116449#post116449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking as someone who's played a character with Vanish...it wasn't quite all it was cracked up to be. By the mechanics, all Vanish really does is levy a -5 penalty on sight-based Perception rolls. Sure, if you get into combat, the opponents use the &quot;Fighting Blind&quot; rules, but I never really found the Gift (by RAW) to really feel like it lived up to what the description of the Gift was selling. Other 5-dot Gifts were much more powerful - although of course, any Gift can come in useful in the right circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. I loved Vanish. I suppose it has to do a bit with play style how useful that Gift is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116449#post116449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When we saw the Gifts draft, I took an old character of mine and re-did his Gifts based on his Renown. Not only did he end up having more Gifts/Facets due to the way Auspice Gifts work now, overall his Gifts had a tighter and more thematic focus. He lost some stuff, but gained new abilities that are far more evocative of a hunting wolf. And as the character is a Hunter in Darkness Elodoth, that very much fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds seriously great. And I hope you cut out a lot of the dead weight. Lots of Gifts were, frankly, narrow to the point of uselessness, or simply didn't give enough bonus to mandate the use of an action, or the cost of activating it. I'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116449#post116449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hunting and Changing Gifts are pretty cool, but I'm afraid I can't speak particulars on them quite yet. Chris may be able to say more whenever he's back to his computer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm waiting eagerly!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116449#post116449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there is any lack of clarity, that's what redlines and playtesting are for - to find those and clear them up. Thanks for pointing it out!</div> </div> </div> </div>Wohoo! I helped!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T06:51:56-07:00","id":116481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116472#post116472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing that was kinda unclear. Does one have to buy the Gift as a whole, before one can start picking Facets from it, or can you just decide &quot;Nah, now I want the Cunning Facet of... Hmm. That list way, way over there.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to let Chris answer that, so as to not steal his thunder. If I do that, should either of us ever cross the pond, I might get something heavy thrown at my head. Maybe. I don't know. Or I'm making that up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116472#post116472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, when you raise Renown, do you have to stay within Affinity?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure, yes. That's how I did it when reworking my previous character. It makes sense to me to do it that way, anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116472#post116472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I know, I know. I was merely commenting on first looks. I think the Shadow Gifts we saw were a bit weak compared to the powers of Demons and Vampires, is mostly all. The Moon Gifts are awesome though, if a tad expensive at the end.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm looking forward to seeing all of the bits all together. So far, though, I don't think there will be a problem overall.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116472#post116472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, White Room fights are rarely useful, but it might be worth considering how much one has to stack a fight to make it come out in one's favour. The physical disciplines of the vampires are crazy strong. Which I like, I might add. I just want werewolves to be on par with that. While having to rely on one's pack for fights is extremely thematic, it isn't very fun to be forced into it. Cooperation should be a strength, not a requirement. At least in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116472#post116472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah. I loved Vanish. I suppose it has to do a bit with play style how useful that Gift is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't get me wrong - I loved Vanish too. The mechanics just didn't live up to the fluff exactly. Now, I played in the Cam (now MES), so the Addendum simply changed the rules on it. I think the rules changed to something much, much better, but hey, I didn't make that rule, so I just played by it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116472#post116472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds seriously great. And I hope you cut out a lot of the dead weight. Lots of Gifts were, frankly, narrow to the point of uselessness, or simply didn't give enough bonus to mandate the use of an action, or the cost of activating it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really did, actually. I mean, I could have taken a particular Gift over again in its Facet form, but I chose a different Facet instead. The thing about my character was that he as only a mediocre Elodoth at best (and even then, was very spirit-centric, or an Envoy if one uses Signs of the Moon), but he was a very good Hunter in Darkness. His new power set reflects that dangerously well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116472#post116472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wohoo! I helped!</div> </div> </div> </div>*internet cookie* <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Honestly, I can't speak for anyone else on what gets changed between now and the final. I can only change my stuff based on what redlines I get back from Stew. Now, we certainly give each other feedback on stuff and share opinions (seriously, this team is a pretty damn good working environment), but final stuff on this is up to Chris and Stew. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T07:14:26-07:00","id":116488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116418#post116418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Please, PLEASE, explain me - will werewolves have powers wich equal to 5-dot Disciplines or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>So far only for Moon Gifts , and from the examples given here , they won't be as powerful , just a bit more shiny .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","name":"Furry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T07:39:01-07:00","id":116495,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Stew</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#888888\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><i>April 19, 2014 at 11:06 am</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Having a 4- or 5-dot equivalent Gift doesn\u2019t make sense under the new system.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> I understand that the new experience system with bits works differently , but vampire already has an increasing rate of super powers according to the old recipe , you still buy them with normal xp cost (which is not an increasing one for higher levels of a discipline list) . Werewolves on the other hand buy two powers with a single dot of Renown , but only one has increased power effects . Werewolves win more flexibility but lack of higher power . That confuses me a lot especially when taking Mage in consideration , still I don't have the whole image , but so far I believe that the whole system will be a great success or a total disappointment , depending on the rest elements the game contains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2194,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","user":"Furry","date":". 04-20-2014, 10:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","name":"Furry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T08:03:09-07:00","id":116500,"title":"","content":"Remember guys, Gifts are not the only special powers Werewolves will get. At MINIMUM we know there's still forms, rituals, and merits to come, and there may still be more we don't know about yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T08:19:33-07:00","id":116507,"title":"","content":"Oh, and Fetishes. And totems, and what ever other benefits you might get from being in a pack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T08:26:25-07:00","id":116509,"title":"","content":"I love the new gifts, I actually feel that they encourage a pack to choose gifts that synergize with each other. A lot of threats that the Uratha face are stronger then them individually, and the Uratha need to ban together to face them.<br /> <br /> As and example, I can totally see the shenanigans a Elodoth and Irraka could pull off with Nature's Lure and Knotted Paths. A Irraka brings prey into a clearing were a ambush is lying in wait, and the Elodoth keeps them from escaping via Knotted Paths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T09:12:15-07:00","id":116534,"title":"","content":"Oh man, I hope we get a beta document for playtesting. I know at least 5 people that'd like to run with these.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T12:30:07-07:00","id":116633,"title":"","content":"If nothing else came out of this, Technology suddenly sounds amazing where as before I laughed at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T13:03:49-07:00","id":116651,"title":"","content":"Yeah, in the end, &quot;power level&quot; is still going to be a big thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T13:41:27-07:00","id":116669,"title":"","content":"I'm not worried about power level at this point-I'm a Changeling player, and if you listened to the original commentators on that the entire splat was underpowered(it sort of is, but I never had a problem with it).<br /> <br /> I assume that when you buy a Gift, you do get at least one free Facet with it.<br /> <br /> My current worry is more related to that entire &quot;different shades of the same thing&quot; I mentioned about when I talked about Technology-nature has some of it too, even if it's easy to see it stringing together.<br /> <br /> ...And yeah, Someone mentioned Werewolves having something equal to the Physical Disciplines of B&amp;S? I wouldn't object to that either, but we'll see how it turns out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T13:52:43-07:00","id":116673,"title":"","content":"Arc: Can you imagine what the Strength Gift is gonna be like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T13:57:55-07:00","id":116675,"title":"","content":"Dunno if I'd want something equivalent to the physical disciplines, exactly, but WtF did have some nice, passive bonus gifts. Like Blood Moon, giving you a penalty to Kuruth but a bonus to all the physical stats in gauru. I really liked these, and the ability to just get a gift that doesn't have to be activated, but improves you one way or another, is a really nice touch. Maybe one werewolf's teeth continuously drip with poison, while another has claws that can go through inorganic substances, and another can always see in the dark, etc.<br /> <br /> Flat out duplicating physical disciplines seems a lazy way to do it.<br /> <br /> I'm a changeling player as well, and they at least had a lot of, 'hands off, this is ours alone,' stuff with the Hedge and pledges, and some Goblin contracts are amazing.<br /> <br /> Despite being half-spirit, the only benefit you get for that is the more powerful you are, the more likely you are to fall comatose unless you move into the Shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-20-2014, 07:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T15:01:44-07:00","id":116692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116675#post116675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Despite being half-spirit, the only benefit you get for that is the more powerful you are, the more likely you are to fall comatose unless you move into the Shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div> Can you please expand on what you mean by that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T15:34:18-07:00","id":116700,"title":"","content":"As your Primal Urge goes up, you start bleeding essence, losing it at a slow rate (at first, 1 a day), to every few hours as long as you are in the real world. Once you lose all your essence, you fall into a comatose state until you're fed essence, or placed in a locus, where you'll wake up in 24 hours.<br /> <br /> Whether you like hanging around the Shadow or not, this is not a benefit in any way.<br /> <br /> In addition with Primal Urge, you gain a social penalty for all social rolls against humans that increases as you raise it (which I imagine is being removed, considering the increased interactivity with humans the Irraka gifts suggest).<br /> <br /> I imagine at some point they were planning on delving into what you become as you become more spiritual, but outside of Renown, you always remain an unwanted part of the Shadow realm while a not exactly fitting in member of the real world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T15:34:44-07:00","id":116701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116692#post116692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Can you please expand on what you mean by that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he means the Essence loss of high Primal Urge werewolves, when they don't go to the shadow frequently enough. I agree that high Primal Urge werewolves could have used some more bonusses to offset this and the social penalty, and to show that they are more primal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T15:48:10-07:00","id":116703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116700#post116700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As your Primal Urge goes up, you start bleeding essence, losing it at a slow rate (at first, 1 a day), to every few hours as long as you are in the real world. Once you lose all your essence, you fall into a comatose state until you're fed essence, or placed in a locus, where you'll wake up in 24 hours.<br /> <br /> Whether you like hanging around the Shadow or not, this is not a benefit in any way.<br /> <br /> In addition with Primal Urge, you gain a social penalty for all social rolls against humans that increases as you raise it (which I imagine is being removed, considering the increased interactivity with humans the Irraka gifts suggest).<br /> <br /> I imagine at some point they were planning on delving into what you become as you become more spiritual, but outside of Renown, you always remain an unwanted part of the Shadow realm while a not exactly fitting in member of the real world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though if Idigam Chronicels does for Werewolf what Blood and Smoke did for Vampire, Primal Urge will not be such a terrible stat to increase. My guess is we'll have to wait for the week that teases Primal Urge or the base Werewolf Template features to really be sure. Non the less, I feel confident that Werewolves will get the same sorta improvement/base line &quot;shot in the arm&quot; that Vampires got.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T16:24:29-07:00","id":116720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116669#post116669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not worried about power level at this point-I'm a Changeling player, and if you listened to the original commentators on that the entire splat was underpowered(it sort of is, but I never had a problem with it).<br /> <br /> I assume that when you buy a Gift, you do get at least one free Facet with it.<br /> <br /> My current worry is more related to that entire &quot;different shades of the same thing&quot; I mentioned about when I talked about Technology-nature has some of it too, even if it's easy to see it stringing together.<br /> <br /> ...And yeah, Someone mentioned Werewolves having something equal to the Physical Disciplines of B&amp;S? I wouldn't object to that either, but we'll see how it turns out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have a problem in general of one archetype being more powerful than another, what I really care about is does the specific archetype, in this case Werewolf, feel unique and able to do things better in their respective areas. It was one thing I really don't like about the game in its' current state since a Spirit/Life mage can essentially be a better werewolf.<br /> <br /> I am curious what you mean about different shades of the same thing however. I don't quite follow<br /> <br /> Also, on the subject of Werewolves having something equal to the B&amp;S physical disciplines, I don't really want them to have something similar. What I really want is for them to at least have powers not completely related to the Sacred Hunt. If every gift revolves around that, it gets a little annoying. For example, while Majesty might be great for a social oriented vampire, they can use it in political areas, making an entire cult devoted to them, or even trying to pick up a chick at the bar.<br /> <br /> If I have a power that is really only useful for hunting, if I don't want to hunt, I can't use it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T16:48:20-07:00","id":116737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116700#post116700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As your Primal Urge goes up, you start bleeding essence, losing it at a slow rate (at first, 1 a day), to every few hours as long as you are in the real world. Once you lose all your essence, you fall into a comatose state until you're fed essence, or placed in a locus, where you'll wake up in 24 hours.<br /> <br /> Whether you like hanging around the Shadow or not, this is not a benefit in any way.<br /> <br /> In addition with Primal Urge, you gain a social penalty for all social rolls against humans that increases as you raise it (which I imagine is being removed, considering the increased interactivity with humans the Irraka gifts suggest).<br /> <br /> I imagine at some point they were planning on delving into what you become as you become more spiritual, but outside of Renown, you always remain an unwanted part of the Shadow realm while a not exactly fitting in member of the real world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for explaining. Without going into detail, I hope as Stew's future teasers are released you'll be pleased.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T16:56:38-07:00","id":116741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116720#post116720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I have a power that is really only useful for hunting, if I don't want to hunt, I can't use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The werewolf mindset sees everything in terms of a hunt. Not a sacred hunt, but every action and interaction is a hunt. Hunts don't have to end with blood and death, but they have a goal and the werewolf works towards this 'kill'.<br /> <br /> The utility of Gifts expands when viewing the world through this werewolf lens.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T20:03:58-07:00","id":116811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116673#post116673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arc: Can you imagine what the Strength Gift is gonna be like?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can imagine it turning out a few ways. Some are awesome, some are not.<br /> <br /> I have faith in the former, but in the end it's about waiting and seeing.<br /> <br /> But damn, I wish they had sampled the Gibbous Moon Gifts-Being a Cahalith/Iron Master fan, I'd have loved seeing samples on both scores. EDIT: Actually, if I'm honest with myself, I'm making another character in this variation, and wanted the Gibbous Moon to just see where it would go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-20-2014, 11:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T20:26:05-07:00","id":116812,"title":"","content":"I feel so stereotypical for liking Rahu Blood Talons...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1198-devil-bunny","name":"devil bunny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T20:32:16-07:00","id":116813,"title":"","content":"My first love/character for the World of Darkness ever was a Rahu Blood Talon. I still feel fondly for his poorly written ass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T21:32:58-07:00","id":116821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116813#post116813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My first love/character for the World of Darkness ever was a Rahu Blood Talon. I still feel fondly for his poorly written ass.</div> </div> </div> </div>I very we'll may be drunk right now (not really) but this literally had me in tears after reading it from the hilarity. At least it isn't as bad as my first character named Eric Erickson who was a werewolf boxer and used boxing instead of ya know...claws. I didn't even take the boxing merits and kept trying to act like a human with morality 7.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T08:25:26-07:00","id":116959,"title":"","content":"May be it\u2019s would be better provide a combined system? For example, if there will be some Battle gifts, the Pure Battle give bonus dices to attack (for example, your highest Renown), while Cunning Battle let you ignore enemy\u2019s Defence and Wisdom Battle let you analyze the stats of one of your enemy (just see its char-list, at least those stats, which can be used for fight).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T10:32:36-07:00","id":117027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116741#post116741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The werewolf mindset sees everything in terms of a hunt. Not a sacred hunt, but every action and interaction is a hunt. Hunts don't have to end with blood and death, but they have a goal and the werewolf works towards this 'kill'.<br /> <br /> The utility of Gifts expands when viewing the world through this werewolf lens.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But then, that mindset is not unique to Idigam Chronicles. After all, it was the core theme in Standard Werewolf the Forsaken. The wolf MUST hunt, after all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T10:51:56-07:00","id":117037,"title":"","content":"Werewolf's theme was more, 'hunt or be hunted,' and as we've established (I hope), the gifts were pretty scattershot in focus, ranging from ultraspecialized to 'what does this have to do with anything?'<br /> <br /> They're clearly working on tightening things up, but considering the gifts are only in their first draft and we haven't seen them all, let alone all their abilities, I'd suggest waiting for more evidence before deciding that powers are useless.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, anyone have any theories about the Pure? Going with the tribes spoiler, think they'd focus their beliefs on 'hunt the weak, hunt the impure, and hunt the faithless?'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-21-2014, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T11:24:41-07:00","id":117057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=117037#post117037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, anyone have any theories about the Pure? Going with the tribes spoiler, think they'd focus their beliefs on 'hunt the weak, hunt the impure, and hunt the faithless?'</div> </div> </div> </div>That would work for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T11:25:15-07:00","id":117058,"title":"","content":"Perhaps, <i><b>Nofather</b></i>, but then, I never had any issues with Previous Gifts at all, so YMMV. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> And even though <i><b>Pendragon's </b></i>reworking of them was most excellent, I never used them, because I liked the originals. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T12:52:33-07:00","id":117108,"title":"","content":"Now I notice the new gifts look more like numena <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","name":"Furry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T13:14:33-07:00","id":117118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Furry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=117108#post117108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I notice the new gifts look more like numena <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>...How so?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T13:28:47-07:00","id":117129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=117118#post117118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...How so?</div> </div> </div> </div>a) They have no power level (minus exceptions)<br /> b) Their lists are based on spirit origin (shadow) rather than raw theme (aka ''gift of strength'' rather than ''strength gift list'').<br /> c) Wider variety rather than strict path of choice .<br /> d) Also the previous reasons can easily allow a story teller to convert numena to gifts and vice versa.<br /> e) Gifts of Shadow rather than , spirit gifts .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2194,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","user":"Furry","date":". 04-21-2014, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","name":"Furry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T13:36:17-07:00","id":117134,"title":"","content":"Seems like entirely superficial similarities to me. *shrug* YMMV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T13:40:01-07:00","id":117136,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't necessarily make that connection, but I could see it. The gift being, well, a gift, similar to a numina and you being able to use it in different ways depending upon your renown (though this would imply that your renown are not merely tattoos representing your triumphs as much as some sort of core part of your being).<br /> I believe somewhere in the books it does say werewolf can learn numina, but it may have just been me inferring that.<br /> <br /> I think I preferred someone else's comparison with Geist's keys and manifestations, but that may just be because I liked Geist's power system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-21-2014, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T13:52:03-07:00","id":117140,"title":"","content":"Now I really disappointed in new gifts, couse I really don't understand, how it help you in high level fights? When vampire with 5-dot discipline try to kill your werewolf, what you will do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T14:06:13-07:00","id":117151,"title":"","content":"Kill them back?<br /> <br /> Considering we've been dealing with dotless powers for a while now that have kicked ass within the WoD in other lines, I find it really weird so many people are hopped up on worry now that we're back to something that had dots, but is, in all honesty, becoming a dotless system, particularly since the power scales of these have been all over the board to begin with, as described by countless people here. Forsaken's gifts were very patchwork, with several 5 dots not being any more efficient than other lines 3 dots. And it becomes worse when we think of it like a pissing match between templates.<br /> <br /> Game Balance is a Myth, let's remember that to begin with. Secondly, Let's not make hasty conclusions about where the line is going with it's utility based on a preview designed to show overall function and the feel of Gifts of the whole. Third, remember that Vampire used to be tremendously nerfed in so many ways, and then Blood and Smoke came along and made them badasses. Idigam is out to accomplish the same, with the same general weight of years behind it. The trend towards improvement that has been heralded since the introduction of the God Machine Chronicle towards improvement in general is a positive one, so it's best to sit down, relax, enjoy what we have, comment on the problems with what we see(as opposed to what we don't), and wait for what comes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T14:16:20-07:00","id":117157,"title":"","content":"It seems very weird to me that auspice gifts are tiered whereas other gifts aren't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T14:21:02-07:00","id":117160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=117134#post117134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems like entirely superficial similarities to me. *shrug* YMMV.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nyah they have the same origin and come from the same realm and same entities .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=117140#post117140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I really disappointed in new gifts, couse I really don't understand, how it help you in high level fights? When vampire with 5-dot discipline try to kill your werewolf, what you will do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits kick vampire ass with dotless numena , so I guess werewolves will kick the same pieces of ass with same ease by using dotless gifts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2194,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","user":"Furry","date":". 04-21-2014, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","name":"Furry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T14:35:20-07:00","id":117172,"title":"","content":"That's also assuming the vampire has a 5 dot ability that stops the garou form from rending them in half like a straw doll. Remember we haven't seen the form bonuses yet, and Garou form and Kuruth both got a rework if I read that correctly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T14:38:36-07:00","id":117176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=117157#post117157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems very weird to me that auspice gifts are tiered whereas other gifts aren't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. There's really no reason why they have to be either, exponential experience costs are out and the powers don't grow out of one another the way Disciplines or Arcana do. Plus I think it'd look more elegant and inspire greater character diversity if they dropped the dot progression entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T14:43:38-07:00","id":117181,"title":"","content":"Since Stew has offered Forms and Kuruth as voting choices, it's safe to say he has things he wants to share with everyone.<br /> <br /> As for what you'd do when a vampire attacks, you'd use Gifts, Fetishes, Form and Pack, same as always. You'd try to turn the tables on him, remove his advantages, make him the prey. Context always matters - white room scenarios are rarely useful.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T15:19:02-07:00","id":117194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=117136#post117136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't necessarily make that connection, but I could see it. The gift being, well, a gift, similar to a numina and you being able to use it in different ways depending upon your renown (though this would imply that your renown are not merely tattoos representing your triumphs as much as some sort of core part of your being).<br /> I believe somewhere in the books it does say werewolf can learn numina, but it may have just been me inferring that.<br /> <br /> I think I preferred someone else's comparison with Geist's keys and manifestations, but that may just be because I liked Geist's power system.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was me. If you think about it, there are a lot of similarities, with Gifts and Manifestations being the general type of power and Keys and Renown being the thing that &quot;unlocks&quot; what specific form your powers take. The main difference is with Geist it's the powers themselves that are tiered and with Werewolf its the Renown that's tiered and the Gifts get more powerful based on which Renown Facet you use them with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T16:03:55-07:00","id":117215,"title":"","content":"I hope that werewolves will make combo using different Facet and it's give them abilities equal to high-level powers. Becouse without it they will be just scum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2297,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","user":"TheBadWolf","date":". 04-21-2014, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T16:20:10-07:00","id":117220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780