.<br /> <br /> Hell, I'd be surprised if their Three Dot Gift doesn't allow the transfer of 3 Dot Moon Gift effects to all packmates. With the 5-Dot literally causing all of them to share the same essence, willpower, <b>and health levels</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Augh! No Corsican Brothers!!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T12:00:15-07:00","id":117563,"title":"","content":"It was bad idea to choose gifts. I mean now we still know nothing, but personaly I'm afraid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T12:29:55-07:00","id":117573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=117563#post117563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was bad idea to choose gifts. I mean now we still know nothing, but personaly I'm afraid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Afraid...really? Overreaction much? <br /> <br /> Its not like the first draft of gifts has completely destroyed the basic idea of what a Werewolf game is. <br /> <br /> You know, since your argument so far seems to be that you feel that because the <b>majority</b> (as in not all just most) of Gifts are now equivalent to 3 dot powers Werewolves are &quot;underpowered&quot; or something. Important to note that the writers have put the caveat that certain gifts are going to be stronger and more like 4 or 5 dot powers. Just that those sorts of gift are going to be rarer then they were in the older version of Forsaken. <br /> <br /> Despite the fact that even with the minimal first draft version info we have Werewolves are starting with at least 5 gifts. Giving them far more versatility then Vampires (who get three discipline dots) or Demons (who get 4 embeds or 3 embeds and an exploit). <br /> <br /> This is before we know anything about the 4 other areas that Werewolves draw power from - Forms, Rites, Fetishes and Merits. Personally it looks to me like Idigam Chronicle Werewolves might have the sort of power synergy we've only seen in Changeling so far. Which is frightening when it gets going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T12:54:50-07:00","id":117580,"title":"","content":"Right, I am now back from a weekend in a field with 1,500 other people in a field in Buckinghamshire <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Am absolutely knackered, but will try to get round to answering some of the questions and queries in this thread, although I note Stew has already covered a few with his replies to the article itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T13:05:42-07:00","id":117589,"title":"","content":"WhaT I have noticed so far is that werewolf is the avant garde of WoD series . Always the first game that players see new things going on and this is one of the things I LOOOVE in this game . I have made a small discussion with my players and they like the idea of no level powers , since it is closer to the wolf-hunter theme of the game , I agree with that . The problem I still have is with crossover power clash , and mostly with Mage which is the most misanderstood game of the WoD line . Vampire-Werewolf Cross , was never a problem , since vampires were the weakest and the poorest of the critters in mystical options , which now has been fixed alot with Stryx Chronicle . But Mage had it's issues ... let's wait and see where it will go . SO far the werewolf development shows that it will be the best werwolf game ever been created , but the completion of the project shall show if it will stand alone or toe-to-toe with the rest of the series , <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","name":"Furry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T13:25:55-07:00","id":117595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really hope, that werewolf with PU 10 will be strong enough to fightagainst vampire with BP 10 is really humiliating, if they do not</div> </div> </div> </div>Really not the point of WoD games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T13:27:05-07:00","id":117598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=117546#post117546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really hope, that Devide and Conqure woulds be changed, cause now it's really strange and useless, if we speaks not about fools. If someone one moves away from the group, the others must immediately ask, &quot;Hey, where are you?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And then they spend the next few minutes arguing. How is that bad for you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T13:35:20-07:00","id":117604,"title":"","content":"Having read through the thread, before I go about putting a few answers to questions out there, I do have to say that perhaps had the Strength, Rage or Elemental Gifts been teased then a lot of concerns would probably have been quelled.<br /> <br /> Although then I'm sure you'd have had a totally different set of concerns having not seen the Nature and Technology Gifts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, suffice to say that if you're concerned about the raw physical potency of werewolves, please understand that Nature and Technology aren't really <i>about</i> that, and that there are all sorts of moving parts in the system that will interact in fairly terrifying ways. Take a Rahu with a few dots of Purity, mix in some Facets out of Strength and Rage and season with a hefty sprinkling of Gauru form. That's not something you want to get in the way of, nor something you can easily <i>stop</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T13:46:29-07:00","id":117614,"title":"","content":"I have a question Acrozatarim. <br /> <br /> One of the issues I had with the old Gift lists was that Gifts were very unfocused and frankly contained a lot of powers I did not feel were very &quot;Werewolf&quot; themed and more just sorta generic magic powers that one expects from a Major template in the WoD. <br /> <br /> However, since these new Chronicle books seem to be trying to focus powers more along the themes of the Supernatural creatures in question I've noticed a change in that. Vampire has always been the most focused game thematically when it comes to its powers (at least in core) so I was not surprised when Blood and Smoke just reinforced the trend already in the games previously published material. <br /> <br /> Idigam is obviously themed around the idea of &quot;the hunt&quot; which is a great idea for getting powers more in line with what I feel is thematically &quot;Werewolf&quot; like. I have to ask though, with Gifts like Technology (though I do understand the idea of &quot;removing the prey's tools&quot; as a sorta way to tie it into hunting) and Elements how do you apply the theme of &quot;the hunt&quot;? As these were some of the powers I found most &quot;un-Werewolf&quot; like in the old book. <br /> <br /> Even with this first draft I'm not entirely sold on the idea of Werewolves as apex predators/hunters having the ability to say make a machine fall apart. Maybe its because its not something I associate with Werewolf media or myth. Still, I'm very interested in hearing your take on trying to apply Werewolf themes to something that seems &quot;not very Werewolf&quot; when first presented. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T13:55:59-07:00","id":117624,"title":"","content":"It's bad couse other part of group will go with target. Or don't let target go. I mean, werewolves must fight against something more than usuall Jason Voorhees' forder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2297,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","user":"TheBadWolf","date":". 04-22-2014, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T14:27:17-07:00","id":117645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=117624#post117624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's bad couse other part of group will go with target. Or don't let target go. I mean, werewolves must fight against something more than usuall Jason Voorhees' forder.</div> </div> </div> </div> We don't even know what the Condition does yet. For all we know, it might make the victim insist on going off alone to the point of fighting his teammates if they try to follow him. Or it might not, we don't know yet. Please stop assuming the worst case scenario when we have hardly any information to go on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T14:42:26-07:00","id":117654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=117645#post117645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please stop assuming the worst case scenario when we have hardly any information to go on.</div> </div> </div> </div>To repeat:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idle suggestion to all concerned to not bother with somebody whose literal entire posting body so far consists of complaining about power level in arbitrary terms. Productive discussion is not to be found in that direction and there's less boring things to do with one's time.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T15:16:04-07:00","id":117682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=117624#post117624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's bad couse other part of group will go with target. Or don't let target go. I mean, werewolves must fight against something more than usuall Jason Voorhees' forder.</div> </div> </div> </div>TheBadWolf -You appear to be feeding your own concerns by focusing on white room scenarios without context.<br /> <br /> To use your example above - perhaps the werewolves are hunting a coordinated group that are not 'Jason Voorhees' fodder', as you you put it. So what? The Gift is still not useless, as you claim. How big is this group? Where are they located? What are they doing?<br /> <br /> Suppose we have a group of around 6 individuals. The Irraka uses it on one and that person tries to split off. What is the group going to do about it? Okay, they all follow him like you suggest - that means *all of them* have left whatever safe place they may have established. It also appears that all of them are now focused on trying to stay with an individual who is* clearly trying to get away from them*. That means he's not just wandering zombie-like while they slowly follow. This person wants to get away from his group, and he'll try to do that. He'll run, dart down side streets and alleys, shut doors behind him, tip over bins, make distractions. Whatever. He will try to get away and his group is now wasting its time trying to stay with him and not watching for the werewolves.<br /> <br /> Or the group 'doesn't let him go', as you suggest. How? He wants to go. He's not going to stop just because you ask. He will keep trying to separate. So what does the group do about it? If they're in a locked room he'll unlock it to escape. Will they restrain him? That's going to take at least one group member, maybe more, to wrestle him to the ground. Group members who are no longer watching their defences. They've got him on the ground, no what? He keeps struggling, and they have to stay on him. Or he pretends to come to his senses, and as soon as they let him go, he tries to escape again. So then what? They knock him out, or tie him up? That's one less defender for the group, and one more useless person they have to protect - if the location is compromised, someone has to carry the guy. That slows them down.<br /> <br /> Or let's say the group does follow the affected character and sticks together, however difficult. The Irraka targets a second character who is lured. Now the group splits in two . Both of those characters who are trying to get away from the group *will* go in different directions. They will separate the group. You now have two groups of three, and one person out of each of those three is actively trying to get away from the other two.<br /> <br /> And all of this assumes the Irraka *uses nothing except that one Gift*.<br /> <br /> You are making blanket statements about white room scenarios and not thinking through how your own examples would actually work in play. I believe that is causing your anxiety. Please don't worry, and understand that people have only seen a small slice of what it coming so far.<br /> <br /> Satchel - last attempt, I promise <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T15:16:14-07:00","id":117683,"title":"","content":"Also, since it is an ambush capability, your likely using it on people that aren't expecting trouble more often than those that are.<br /> <br /> Essentially TheBadWolf, your making a mountain out of a molehill with whatifs.<br /> <br /> What if the one you pull away is a blood potency 10 vampire that had the worst luck on resisting, but then will go on to throwing 40+ dice with each attack? Lets not play what-ifs on rough drafts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T15:23:08-07:00","id":117688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=117614#post117614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idigam is obviously themed around the idea of &quot;the hunt&quot; which is a great idea for getting powers more in line with what I feel is thematically &quot;Werewolf&quot; like. I have to ask though, with Gifts like Technology (though I do understand the idea of &quot;removing the prey's tools&quot; as a sorta way to tie it into hunting) and Elements how do you apply the theme of &quot;the hunt&quot;? As these were some of the powers I found most &quot;un-Werewolf&quot; like in the old book.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You've certainly hit on one of (many) challenges I was faced with when drafting up the new Gifts. At some point I'll try and bolt together a little design piece about some of the goals and design decisions I made on the wider level, but suffice to say that I was happy to have the lists of Facets spread their wings slightly into more shamanic or spiritual areas with some of the Gifts. This is especially true of Elemental, which is a slightly more experimental take on Gift structure than the others in Idigam.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, Technology is one of the core Gift lists, so I looked to concepts of dominance, depriving the prey of the tools they rely on and animistic interaction with the modern world. It's the Iron Masters' signature Gift and their tribal prey is the one that most relies on technology, so in many ways Technology is a Gift of exploiting the world of humans through the devices that they rely on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T15:27:22-07:00","id":117689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=117604#post117604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, suffice to say that if you're concerned about the raw physical potency of werewolves, please understand that Nature and Technology aren't really <i>about</i> that, and that there are all sorts of moving parts in the system that will interact in fairly terrifying ways. Take a Rahu with a few dots of Purity, mix in some Facets out of Strength and Rage and season with a hefty sprinkling of Gauru form. That's not something you want to get in the way of, nor something you can easily <i>stop</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a heck of a true story, sir. Actually, it's damned terrifying to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T15:30:22-07:00","id":117692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=117688#post117688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the Iron Masters' signature Gift and their tribal prey is the one that most relies on technology, so in many ways Technology is a Gift of exploiting the world of humans through the devices that they rely on.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026Cross-applying this to the Hunters and the Hosts, suddenly Knotted Paths takes on a whole new degree of utility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T15:45:15-07:00","id":117699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=117689#post117689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is a heck of a true story, sir. Actually, it's damned terrifying to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Troo storee: I had a look at some of the old stats for battle-field scale weaponry from Armory like tank shells and I'm fairly sure you can build a Rahu against whom, while in Gauru with the right Facets, <i>a tank is not sufficient firepower</i>. That's cross-GMC-rules-update of course, but I really, really don't have any worries about combat-specialised werewolves not holding their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T15:47:22-07:00","id":117700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=115803#post115803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will I like what I see of the gifts themselves I'm still wondering whether or not it will make werewolves as much of an XP sink as before. I like that it's already reduced somewhat by not having an out of order XP hike anymore but that was just the tip of the iceberg. I guess we won't know until we see actual numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I ran several Werewolf games and I know your pain around XP sinks in Forsaken. The cost in Experiences is something we're still hammering away at, and I wouldn't be surprised if it doesn't get tweaked and amended further during playtesting. It's something I really want to get right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T15:55:45-07:00","id":117705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NeoTiamat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=115867#post115867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Color me unenthused.<br /> <br /> Well, no, that's not entirely fair. These are generally much better than the old Gifts. That said, two points/concerns:<br /> <br /> 1) I'm saddened that we are still stuck with Renown, which seems like an unnecessary layer of complexity and an artificial speed bump in character development.<br /> 2) The fact that the first gift I see is &quot;perfect, unstoppable lie-detection&quot; makes me weep. So basically... social shenanigans do not work if there's an Elodoth in the party. Lovely.</div> </div> </div> </div>On 1), I always found Renown a bit of a burden in the original W:tF system. The high XP costs and the rather tacked-on way that it affected things like Gifts just annoyed me. That said, we're working on integrating it better in IC, and I've worked a bit on the metaphysics of how Gifts and Facets operate to render the part that Renown plays into something a bit more evocative.<br /> <br /> On 2) It's not perfect nor unstoppable, being both contested and something that <i>can</i> still be worked around. I can't remember whether it's in this thread or the article comments, but a few methods of working around Scent Beneath The Surface have been mentioned; they require some thought and some set-up but they're not really excessively difficult. The main difference between the new and old Scent is that this one costs Essence and the old cost Willpower, but the old version already offered much of the same thing - of course, if you had a problem with the old one too then fair enough <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> On a side note for the thread in general: Willpower costs are now gone from Facets in general. Where they have an activation cost, it's Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T16:02:17-07:00","id":117709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=117683#post117683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, since it is an ambush capability, your likely using it on people that aren't expecting trouble more often than those that are.</div> </div> </div> </div> If it's some tourists, werewolf no need to use gifts to kill them. I see, for example, Hunters (mortal) group who go through the forest with machine-guns and silver bullets. I think it's much more decent (and more probable) opponent for a pack.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T16:13:38-07:00","id":117717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=117699#post117699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Troo storee: I had a look at some of the old stats for battle-field scale weaponry from Armory like tank shells and I'm fairly sure you can build a Rahu against whom, while in Gauru with the right Facets, <i>a tank is not sufficient firepower</i>. That's cross-GMC-rules-update of course, but I really, really don't have any worries about combat-specialised werewolves not holding their own.</div> </div> </div> </div> Dude, I really, really hope that its work this way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T16:15:40-07:00","id":117718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=115970#post115970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm sure rituals will pick up that slack. And I wouldn't be surprised if there are shaman-y Gifts as well. Crescent moon sounded awesome, starting out letting you see spirits and capping off letting you sense any spirit in a very wide radius and see through any of their senses. I assume that won't be the only Gift that focuses on interacting with spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, Crescent Moon doesn't <i>just</i> let you see spirits at the first dot, it gives you quite a bit more <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that, by and large, Facets that are focused on the hunt work just fine against spirits too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116024#post116024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of this will come down to the expense of Gifts, Facets, and <i>especiall</i><i>y</i> Renown. If the price is right, this is a minor issue, but if it's not, then we have taken a two way EXP sink and turned it into a three way, little-bit-confusing-and-yet-somehow-more-streamlined EXP sink.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that this is one of the pitfalls we face and something we need to get right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nature weird me out a little, given how much city is in it, </div> </div> </div>I was keen to avoid Nature being a Gift that's basically pointless if your Chronicle takes place in the city. There's an awful <i>lot</i> of nature present in the cities and settlements of today, and it felt worth emphasising that, for example, Hunters In Darkness are just as terrifying in a city park or area of urban wasteland as they are out in the wild, dark woods.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Red 9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116051#post116051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I say specificity I'm referring to the general habit of Forsaken powers to have a &quot;This, but not this&quot; setup.</div> </div> </div> </div>A fair number of old arbitrary limits are out. The Gift of Dominance no longer has the old Dominance thing about only working on werewolves and humans; detection Facets, where they exist, are generally up-gunned in what information they provide.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116055#post116055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm concerned with how this system will work with character development, personally. By having the bulk of available Gifts be 3-dot equivalents of different applications, I foresee two related results: Werewolves are going to be really powerful out-of-the-gate, with starting characters able to pull some really nasty tricks; but also once they start gaining exp they're going to have roughly the same power-level, only diversified across a wider range of applications.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can assure you that this will not be the case. Lots of Facets click together in nasty ways or just provide different advantages to the same area of conflict, and there is a scaling element involved as well. Your highly experienced Rahu, for example, will be scarier Facets-wise than his less-experienced Rahu compatriot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T16:22:38-07:00","id":117721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116267#post116267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Scent Beneath the Surface, I would assume that in a later form of it, a supernatural template would probably have a clash of wills or a contested roll of some kind especially if using a power to enhance his social abilities. Keep in mind, this is still a first draft</div> </div> </div> </div>The Clash of Wills rules will be at the beginning of the Gifts section; they work the same way as for Blood &amp; Smoke.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116336#post116336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seem a bit confused. According to the description of Death Gifts it says that both the Rahu and Irakka would gain the wisdom facet of Death's Gift. How does this work? I thought you chose the Gift that gained a Renown's facet.</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify; Stew said that the Wisdom Facet of Death's Gift is useful to both Rahu and Irraka because they're Bone Shadows - hence having Wisdom as their Tribal Renown. It doesn't state that they have to choose the Wisdom Facet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116418#post116418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Please, PLEASE, explain me - will werewolves have powers wich equal to 5-dot Disciplines or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bolting together Facets allows for some very potent results. Some are implicit - activate enough combat-boosting Facets and you're going to have impressive results. Some are explicit, mainly the Gift of the Elements which has a slightly unusual structure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T16:38:24-07:00","id":117727,"title":"","content":"Damn, did I not have it as weirded? Shame on me.<br /> <br /> Anyways, I forgot to mention it while talking about Nature, but while it weirded me out, I was actually really glad to see a change in definition for it. It's still geared towards the traditional thoughts of nature, but the expansion felt thematically appropriate-to a werewolf, everywhere is a deep, dark forest or a wild jungle, and the Gifts they receive reflect that to certain degrees.<br /> <br /> Weird, yes, satisfying, definitely.<br /> <br /> Anyways, I say again: despite some concerns about the presentation of information(it did take me a few reads to be absolutely clear how it all worked) and how the economy for powers works, these Gifts have been thoroughly heartening for me. I quite frankly have nothing but optimism for how this works out.<br /> <br /> Of course, that was before I read about the teases about Strength, Rage, Elemental, and the lot of them.<br /> <br /> And the ability of a Rahu to take on a tank. Now, I'm no longer optimistic.<br /> <br /> I'm better than-I feel just shy of perfect assurance.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You guys know what you're doing, and I don't feel a reason to doubt the turn out.<br /> <br /> And even if it <i>is</i> a failure, it should be a spectacular one regardless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T16:43:50-07:00","id":117729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116422#post116422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Things like Savage Might, Thunderbolt, Vanish and Primal Form were pure terror. Sure, there were many bad 5 dot powers (Most, in fact.), but the solution to that should be fixing the bad ones, not remove them all, should it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Two things I'd say in response to this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The first is a direct reply to your concerns. I genuinely feel that there are plentiful very powerful Facets that will provide the kinda hit that people are looking for, especially when combined; Facets for which you also won't have to churn through four other powers first that you don't necessarily want. Primal Form was alright, but you can do better with the new Facets.<br /> <br /> The second is a more general note for the thread - I got rid of what we termed 'Killing You Gifts'. Things like Thunderbolt and Killing Frost - powers that involve the werewolf pointing and throwing magic at a target to kill them, mage-style - are generally gone. Instead, the new Facets that focus on making the werewolf better at killing make them superior at doing so up close and personal, with claws and teeth and weapons. A werewolf doesn't call lightning down to strike you with a Facet; a Facet gives a werewolf the ability to tear through steel like it was butter, or to hack you apart like a joint of meat with each strike crippling you in a horrific new fashion.<br /> <br /> I have, however, kept Facets with effects under what we classify as the old 'Killing Your City Gifts' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thirdly. Are the Wolf Gifts ONLY the old Father Wolf and Mother Luna gifts? Or do they involve things like Strength and Stealth as well? Since they don't really feel magical in the same way, they are just enhancements of the Uratha in question after all. </div> </div> </div>The Wolf Gifts are, as Stew said, currently just the Hunting and Changing Gifts. Each includes Facets that roll under those particular concepts. Here's a spoiler: Pack Awareness still exists, but now it's a Wolf Gift that anyone can get.<br /> <br /> Stealth and Strength both remain Shadow Gifts.<br /> <br /> In theory we could add more Wolf Gifts in the future. I have rough ideas for a couple, but I won't have the word count space to add them into the IC book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116472#post116472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Another thing that was kinda unclear. Does one have to buy the Gift as a whole, before one can start picking Facets from it, or can you just decide &quot;Nah, now I want the Cunning Facet of... Hmm. That list way, way over there.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You buy a Gift first, unlocking a Facet within it. With Shadow Gifts, this requires more than just a buy-in in Experiences <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Once you've unlocked the Gift, you can freely access new Facets within it by paying the relevant cost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This sounds seriously great. And I hope you cut out a lot of the dead weight. Lots of Gifts were, frankly, narrow to the point of uselessness, or simply didn't give enough bonus to mandate the use of an action, or the cost of activating it. I' </div> </div> </div>As you can see already in the Gifts Stew showed, the bulk of old Gifts have been cut due to being exactly as you say - dead weight. Many live on in new and improved forms under different names, but I haven't been hesitant to just entirely excise those Gifts that frankly weren't very interesting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=116669#post116669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...And yeah, Someone mentioned Werewolves having something equal to the Physical Disciplines of B&amp;S? I wouldn't object to that either, but we'll see how it turns out.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a number of Facets dedicated to making werewolves scary bastards in the physical arena.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T16:57:40-07:00","id":117735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=117729#post117729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a number of Facets dedicated to making werewolves scary bastards in the physical arena.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would it be safe to say then that the IC tries to incorporate the feel of the hunt and the feel of savage fury as the game line suggests? To me, nothing screams Werewolf more than a raging ball of teeth and fur hacking enemies into tiny bits when the time is right.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T18:15:05-07:00","id":117761,"title":"","content":"Can...can there be one Facet called Rules of Nature?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T19:51:35-07:00","id":117804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=117699#post117699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Troo storee: I had a look at some of the old stats for battle-field scale weaponry from Armory like tank shells and I'm fairly sure you can build a Rahu against whom, while in Gauru with the right Facets, <i>a tank is not sufficient firepower</i>. That's cross-GMC-rules-update of course, but I really, really don't have any worries about combat-specialised werewolves not holding their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually hadn't thought of things that way, but now that you mention it...yeah, I can see that. I think I want to see what I can use to kill a werewolf now.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T20:09:46-07:00","id":117809,"title":"","content":"Well looking at your signature I think you have one readily available to you. XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T21:58:51-07:00","id":117855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=117729#post117729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You buy a Gift first, unlocking a Facet within it. With Shadow Gifts, this requires more than just a buy-in in Experiences <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Once you've unlocked the Gift, you can freely access new Facets within it by paying the relevant cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, this was something I was wondering, actually, when I noted the... vagueness... about what &quot;buy-in&quot; might entail. I'm tipping hunting and devouring a related spirit, myself (which I LOVE.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T01:02:41-07:00","id":117886,"title":"","content":"Another small note that may be of interest to people: Blood &amp; Smoke Disciplines cover 38 discrete powers, while there are 110 discrete Facets. Well, 109.5 given one of the Elemental Facets but that's just quibbling really. Unlike the old Gift system with it's ascending ranks of Gifts, the new set-up means there's no place for speed bump powers or powers that are just an improved version of a lower dot Gift. This has interesting results in Gifts like Stealth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T11:57:30-07:00","id":118032,"title":"","content":"Could we have a sentence somewhere declaring that these are not the only gifts in the existence of the universe and storytellers can make their own when appropriate? Unless that's factually untrue or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T12:20:05-07:00","id":118048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=117886#post117886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another small note that may be of interest to people: Blood &amp; Smoke Disciplines cover 38 discrete powers, while there are 110 discrete Facets. Well, 109.5 given one of the Elemental Facets but that's just quibbling really. Unlike the old Gift system with it's ascending ranks of Gifts, the new set-up means there's no place for speed bump powers or powers that are just an improved version of a lower dot Gift. This has interesting results in Gifts like Stealth.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hmm... I'm not sure if I like that... I always prefer fewer powers that are more broadly applicable over more powers that are narrower. Then again, there were always more Gift Lists than (non-bloodline) Disciplines. And I trust you've cut out the useless gifts, so I'm not terribly worried.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T12:36:07-07:00","id":118055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=118032#post118032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could we have a sentence somewhere declaring that these are not the only gifts in the existence of the universe and storytellers can make their own when appropriate? Unless that's factually untrue or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's something along those lines in there already, as we were originally hoping to have the wordcount to do more than one Moon Gift per Auspice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=118048#post118048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hmm... I'm not sure if I like that... I always prefer fewer powers that are more broadly applicable over more powers that are narrower. Then again, there were always more Gift Lists than (non-bloodline) Disciplines. And I trust you've cut out the useless gifts, so I'm not terribly worried.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was really just as a note for people to consider when thinking about thematic foci, etc. It's the same number of Gift powers as were already in the original Forsaken core, it's just that a load of those were 'this lower-dot Gift but better' or plain filler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T12:55:10-07:00","id":118067,"title":"","content":"What about social and mental Giftes and Facets? <br /> <br /> P.S. I like Elodoth gifts, especialy 4th dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T13:18:28-07:00","id":118073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=118055#post118055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think there's something along those lines in there already, as we were originally hoping to have the wordcount to do more than one Moon Gift per Auspice. This was really just as a note for people to consider when thinking about thematic foci, etc. It's the same number of Gift powers as were already in the original Forsaken core, it's just that a load of those were 'this lower-dot Gift but better' or plain filler.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's about what I assumed, but thank you for clarifying. Like I said, I trust you've got a good handle on things. I am very much looking forward to some of these Facet synergies! They sound awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T02:48:55-07:00","id":118352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=118067#post118067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about social and mental Giftes and Facets?<br /> <br /> P.S. I like Elodoth gifts, especialy 4th dot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, there are a number of social and mental Facets; as you'd expect given Gifts like Death, Dominance, Insight, Inspiration and Knowledge <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=118073#post118073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's about what I assumed, but thank you for clarifying. Like I said, I trust you've got a good handle on things. I am very much looking forward to some of these Facet synergies! They sound awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>The number of Facets does mean that a lot of ground is covered, powers-wise. I'm already mulling over a few Gifts that won't be in the corebook and having issues thinking up new mechanics and powers to go into them that aren't already in the new core. I'm very keen to avoid a situation like we have in the current line where there are several different Gifts that all do the same thing (like teleporting through shadows :P).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T02:56:14-07:00","id":118356,"title":"","content":"I have one kinda rules related question, I'm not sure if this has been asked or answered.<br /> <br /> How are Gifts 'learnt' in character now. Is it still a deal with a spirit or is it a more dominance kinda thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/417-the_duck","name":"the_duck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T03:17:11-07:00","id":118358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the_duck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=118356#post118356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have one kinda rules related question, I'm not sure if this has been asked or answered.<br /> <br /> How are Gifts 'learnt' in character now. Is it still a deal with a spirit or is it a more dominance kinda thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm afraid you'll have to wait and see on that front. While I do have an answer, we're still at the first draft stage and there's every chance it will be tweaked and adjusted between now and the final version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T03:39:34-07:00","id":118371,"title":"","content":"I really like the new gifts - but as you say, a couple of them (I mean a couple) feel a bit magey - as in casting a spell from afar - as opposed to visceral bone-&amp;-claw magic. I don't mind the the wisdom ones - the odd nightmares of a sleeping werewolf having horror-movie effects on the real world - is great. I guess I am specifically refering to the Glory facets - shouting at a car to go explodey, or at plants to seize a building. All the otehrs - particularly the cunning and purity ones - feel ideal for a horror chronicle.<br /> <br /> Here's a few ideas on making the Glory ones less magey.<br /> <br /> Nature's Glory: Either some kind of stampede summoning/wild predator summoning (aka the present call to animals but with the caveat - instead of just appearing they attack the target) or the following.<br /> <br /> Twisted Roots: Roots can snare an ankle to trip the Uratha's prey: grass can cover potholes, tussocks shift. Even concrete and cobbles can be slippy with moss or mold; wooden floors cave in, destroyed by rot, at the Uratha's command, as she descends on her victim.<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> Cost: 1 essence<br /> Dicepool: Presence+Survival+Glory-defense<br /> Dramatic Failure: The uratha stumbles herself: She gains the Prone Tilt.<br /> Failure: Roots shift, mold stirs, but not enough to trip anyone.<br /> Success: The plantlife stirs around the targets feet; even on concrete or sheet metal flooring, traces of moss or mould spread subtley to make all footing precarious for the victim. The target gains the Dodgy Footing Condition: he can only move at half speed, rounded down. Any attempts to engage in physical activity - including combat, faster movement etc - suffer a penalty equal to the Uratha's Glory: failure on any roll means the prey falls, gaining the Prone tilt. This lasts for a number of rounds equal to successes.<br /> Exceptional Success: The prey falls prone immediately, and suffers bashing damage equal to successes.<br /> <br /> I could imagine shifting the Technology Glory gift around too: not so it is an &quot;I blast your car from afar&quot; (although the image of a Uratha standing on a bridge and causing car after car to implode is great) but more so it seems like an extension of the beast's power- a wolf's weight, not a mage's blast. Possibly shift the range to touch (including anything that brushes against the uratha/weapons that hit her etc), and to make up for that loss of flexibility, either have it reflexive or make it last a scene (i.e. all weapons/cars/tech the Uratha touches are either destroyed on contact (before damage is resolved) or suffer Glory in Structure damage. Alternately, this could be levied against all weapons targetting the Uratha instead - including guns - but again, that feels a touch like a power-blast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T07:30:50-07:00","id":118417,"title":"","content":"I realize the Spirit aspect of the game seems to be a bit of an onus for some of the fans, but for the other fans who enjoy it, in Idigam Chronicles can werewolves become powerful kings of the spirit world? We've gotten mostly real-world spoilers, and I can appreciate if it can't be answered but the spirit part of the game was a big draw for me to Werewolf the Forsaken, but it never really went all the way, I feel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T07:45:49-07:00","id":118424,"title":"","content":"I'm sure Stew will get to the material about the <i>hisil</i> eventually. It's been changed a bit - this is the fourth time we've explained the basics of the Shadow, after Forsaken, Awakening, and Book of Spirits - and emphasis is different each time. You'll recognise most of it, and maybe be surprised at a few things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T08:34:31-07:00","id":118444,"title":"","content":"I'm fairly content with the general thematics of Unmake - though details are of course likely to get worked on in the next draft - but the Nature Glory Facet is pretty much the one I'm least happy with out of the entire Facet list so far. I would expect that one to look rather different in the final version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T08:55:33-07:00","id":118451,"title":"","content":"Is essence turning into Pyros in terms of fuel recharge because some of these powers are ungodly expensive for their duration.<br /> <br /> Some of these also feel like they should be permanent powers rather than an activated month long duration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-24-2014, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T10:09:51-07:00","id":118478,"title":"","content":"On the essence front, all I believe we've heard so far is that you can get essence from attacking spirits (or something to that extent). No idea if that's still valid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-24-2014, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T10:21:43-07:00","id":118482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=118478#post118478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the essence front, all I believe we've heard so far is that you can get essence from attacking spirits (or something to that extent). No idea if that's still valid.</div> </div> </div> </div> I would assume you can get essence from the siskur-dah","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T13:21:16-07:00","id":118580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=118424#post118424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure Stew will get to the material about the <i>hisil</i> eventually. It's been changed a bit - this is the fourth time we've explained the basics of the Shadow, after Forsaken, Awakening, and Book of Spirits - and emphasis is different each time. You'll recognise most of it, and maybe be surprised at a few things.</div> </div> </div> </div>So far as written in the core book of God Machine Chronicles the only thing that is refered to werewolf-spirit matters was that a werewolf two ranks higher than a spirit he does aggravated to it as if he was its bane .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","name":"Furry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"M