y/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=118590#post118590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Oh I forgot about that... If that makes it into Idigam, that will be badass!</div> </div> </div> </div> Who knows maybe the bane condition will actually become an extended rule in Idigam chronicles .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","name":"Furry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T14:15:38-07:00","id":118628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=118590#post118590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Oh I forgot about that... If that makes it into Idigam, that will be badass!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's still in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T14:34:41-07:00","id":118643,"title":"","content":"Not only that but, as per the rules in the GMC:<br /> - Banes are solid to entities in Twilight and can damage them.<br /> - Banes deal Aggravated damage to Materialised beings and Lethal to beings in Twilight.<br /> <br /> So, going by the GMC rules, spirits aren't safe from werewolves who outrank them even if the spirit is in Twilight. It'll 'only' be Lethal damage but an otherwise ephemeral spirit can still get torn apart by an angry Uratha with enough rank over it.<br /> <br /> Dave, I haven't checked if that's still the case in the first draft of the spirit rules. Up to you if you want to comment further on that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T14:46:25-07:00","id":118648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=118451#post118451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is essence turning into Pyros in terms of fuel recharge because some of these powers are ungodly expensive for their duration.<br /> <br /> Some of these also feel like they should be permanent powers rather than an activated month long duration.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume you mean Binding Oath? I can't see any other month-long durations at a quick glance over the four Gifts that were revealed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T18:11:18-07:00","id":118816,"title":"","content":"I hope the ranking system changes a bit. To be 2 ranks higher than the weakest kind of SpiritRank 1) you need 8 points of renown. That's pretty far from chargen to be a major deal. I hope Rank becomes tied to Primal Urge or the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T18:24:20-07:00","id":118830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=118648#post118648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I assume you mean Binding Oath? I can't see any other month-long durations at a quick glance over the four Gifts that were revealed.</div> </div> </div> </div>There were a few which weren't that long but all the same felt permanent rather than temporary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T20:31:27-07:00","id":118906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=118816#post118816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope the ranking system changes a bit. To be 2 ranks higher than the weakest kind of SpiritRank 1) you need 8 points of renown. That's pretty far from chargen to be a major deal. I hope Rank becomes tied to Primal Urge or the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, pretty much this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T00:07:53-07:00","id":118979,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure tying it to Primal Urge is a big help there. Considering that Primium and Blood Potency both cost 5 Experiences, I don't see Primal Urge being cheaper/making getting higher rank faster being a sufficient method. Though it depends a lot on what the new Renown costs end up being and if the impact of Renown on rank stays the same.<br /> <br /> It's also a bit of a misleading statement to say you need 8 points, because you start with 3 points for free. You need to buy 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T04:55:18-07:00","id":119041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=118830#post118830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There were a few which weren't that long but all the same felt permanent rather than temporary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you mind if I ask you to be more specific? Feedback about this sort of thing really useful but I'm not sure which Facets you're actually referring to <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T05:01:43-07:00","id":119042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=118906#post118906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This, pretty much this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just wrote the Spirit rules. How werewolves calculate their spirit Rank is up to whoever's writing Renown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T04:35:38-07:00","id":121617,"title":"","content":"Nature's Lure seems a bit...specific in it's application. It's got good synergy with some of the other Facets listed, but it seems a little weak on it's own. I'm going to have to scale back the definition of wilderness as well if I run the game. Too many &quot;parks&quot; where I live are just a single tree next to a playground; the idea of a werewolf luring someone into such a thing for an ambush is comical.<br /> <br /> Hopefully we are going to get a better definition of &quot;technology&quot; when things come out. Digital (Computer, Cellphone)? Electronic (Lawnmower, Flashlight)? Mechanical (Rifle, Toilet)? Worked (Knife, Pencil)? Any tool (Rock, Sharp Stick)? If the enemy can't pick up a rock without clobbering themselves in the face with it their pretty screwed. Garble could be &quot;crunchier&quot;. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T11:08:14-07:00","id":121865,"title":"","content":"I have a question and I apologize in advance if it has already been asked elsewhere on these forums. In Blood and Smoke, Kindred were somewhat beefed up, physically, in that most slashing type weapons now cause bashing damage. What of Uratha teeth and claws? Has there been any sort of official ruling on that from Stew and or Rose? My gut feeling is to keep it at lethal, which is what it would have been under the original WtF and VtR rules. But I'd like to have some sort of official (read: play-tested) basis for doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1702-matty1love","name":"Matty1Love","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T12:39:36-07:00","id":121905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matty1Love</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=121865#post121865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question and I apologize in advance if it has already been asked elsewhere on these forums. In Blood and Smoke, Kindred were somewhat beefed up, physically, in that most slashing type weapons now cause bashing damage. What of Uratha teeth and claws? Has there been any sort of official ruling on that from Stew and or Rose? My gut feeling is to keep it at lethal, which is what it would have been under the original WtF and VtR rules. But I'd like to have some sort of official (read: play-tested) basis for doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chris (IIRC) has stated that a Rahu with a few Rage and Strength facets can whistand the assault of a tank and do away with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T12:53:06-07:00","id":121915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=121905#post121905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Chris (IIRC) has stated that a Rahu with a few Rage and Strength facets can whistand the assault of a tank and do away with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate the reply, however, I think you misunderstood the question. My question pertained to whether or not Uratha's natural weaponry: teeth and claws still do lethal damage to VAMPIRES post GMC. The new rules in Blood and Smoke state that knives and other slashing type weapons only do BASHING damage to Kindred. So I was wondering if Uratha claws and teeth would fall in line with that or if they were still considered &quot;lethal&quot; to vampires. Like I said, my assumption would be that they would still do lethal damage. There is a big difference between being stabbed with a knife and having your flesh torn up with razor sharp claws and teeth. But just wanted to make sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1702-matty1love","name":"Matty1Love","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T13:15:54-07:00","id":121933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matty1Love</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=121915#post121915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I appreciate the reply, however, I think you misunderstood the question. My question pertained to whether or not Uratha's natural weaponry: teeth and claws still do lethal damage to VAMPIRES post GMC. The new rules in Blood and Smoke state that knives and other slashing type weapons only do BASHING damage to Kindred. So I was wondering if Uratha claws and teeth would fall in line with that or if they were still considered &amp;quot;lethal&amp;quot; to vampires. Like I said, my assumption would be that they would still do lethal damage. There is a big difference between being stabbed with a knife and having your flesh torn up with razor sharp claws and teeth. But just wanted to make sure.</div> </div> </div> </div> As far as I know, there is no official ruling on this. But I would assume since Dalu, Gauru, and Urshul forms are overtly supernatural, they would be able to do lethal to vampires, while Hishu and Urhan forms are very nearly mundane human and wolf and would therefore do bashing. But your guess is as good as mine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T13:21:26-07:00","id":121938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=121933#post121933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As far as I know, there is no official ruling on this. But I would assume since Dalu, Gauru, and Urshul forms are overtly supernatural, they would be able to do lethal to vampires, while Hishu and Urhan forms are very nearly mundane human and wolf and would therefore do bashing. But your guess is as good as mine.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you use the supernatural argument, though, you could reasonably make an argument that they should do AGGRAVATED damage. That was always one of the things that I found a bit strange about nWoD vamps and werewolves. Werewolf claws do lethal damage to vampires and, but VAMPIRE claws do Aggravated damage. But I guess the argument can also be made that Uratha claws and teeth are more a natural extension of themselves, while donning claws for a vampire requires the use of a discipline. In reality, though, whatever the ruling, it is most certainly going to be made for the sake of balancing the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1702-matty1love","name":"Matty1Love","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T13:38:06-07:00","id":121951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matty1Love</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=121938#post121938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you use the supernatural argument, though, you could reasonably make an argument that they should do AGGRAVATED damage. That was always one of the things that I found a bit strange about nWoD vamps and werewolves. Werewolf claws do lethal damage to vampires and, but VAMPIRE claws do Aggravated damage. But I guess the argument can also be made that Uratha claws and teeth are more a natural extension of themselves, while donning claws for a vampire requires the use of a discipline. In reality, though, whatever the ruling, it is most certainly going to be made for the sake of balancing the game.</div> </div> </div> </div> Protean claws don't do Aggravated any more. They don't even do Lethal to vampires any more until level 4. You can take a Merit to get aggravated claws, but you need Protean 4 as a prerequisite, and then they only deal agg while you're frenzying. Aggravated damage is much more rare now than it was before the update, and the way Vampire's damage reduction works is that mundane sources of lethal deal bashing and mundane sources of Agg deal lethal. Supernatural sources are not downgraded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T15:06:33-07:00","id":122015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=121951#post121951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Protean claws don't do Aggravated any more. They don't even do Lethal to vampires any more until level 4. You can take a Merit to get aggravated claws, but you need Protean 4 as a prerequisite, and then they only deal agg while you're frenzying. Aggravated damage is much more rare now than it was before the update, and the way Vampire's damage reduction works is that mundane sources of lethal deal bashing and mundane sources of Agg deal lethal. Supernatural sources are not downgraded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah! This provides much more context and makes me a bit more comfortable with my assumption. I'm actually a bit embarrassed that I didn't know this being that I OWN Blood and Smoke in hardcover. Just haven't gotten the chance to do more than peruse it at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1702-matty1love","name":"Matty1Love","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T15:27:48-07:00","id":122036,"title":"","content":"The type of damage that werewolf natural weaponry deals to vampires is really something for the Vampire line to cover. I would, however, expect them to be treated the same as other sources of Lethal damage by vampires, ie that they get downgraded to bashing just like swords, axes, bullets etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T17:40:10-07:00","id":122106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=122036#post122036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The type of damage that werewolf natural weaponry deals to vampires is really something for the Vampire line to cover. I would, however, expect them to be treated the same as other sources of Lethal damage by vampires, ie that they get downgraded to bashing just like swords, axes, bullets etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be fine with this. Claws and fangs on their own shouldn't really be overdamaging axes, swords and so forth. Vampires deserve the respect they're due for their undead status and how their bodies are dead things empowered with blood.<br /> <br /> I figure that an insistent werewolf who is knowledgeable in combat will still be a frightening foe to face. But honestly, I would not consider fangs and claws to be the strength werewolves can really leverage to their advantage over vampires...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T17:43:14-07:00","id":122109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=122036#post122036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The type of damage that werewolf natural weaponry deals to vampires is really something for the Vampire line to cover. I would, however, expect them to be treated the same as other sources of Lethal damage by vampires, ie that they get downgraded to bashing just like swords, axes, bullets etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that vampire fangs do lethal even to vampires, which would set a precedent for werewolf bites at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T21:12:20-07:00","id":122182,"title":"","content":"I never get this debate. The Uratha can simply shove a torch on the kindred's face for aggravated damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T03:48:24-07:00","id":122260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=122109#post122109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that vampire fangs do lethal even to vampires, which would set a precedent for werewolf bites at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there's anything particularly special about werewolf bites that should make them deal Lethal to vampires where, for example, a lion's bite just does Bashing.<br /> <br /> Were I to write a crossover patch for IC and B&amp;S, I wouldn't make Uratha natural weapons deal Lethal to Kindred. The Bashing downgrade is one of a vampire's signature defences and werewolves have plenty of other advantages going for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T05:24:25-07:00","id":122275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=122260#post122260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't think there's anything particularly special about werewolf bites that should make them deal Lethal to vampires where, for example, a lion's bite just does Bashing. Were I to write a crossover patch for IC and B&amp;S, I wouldn't make Uratha natural weapons deal Lethal to Kindred. The Bashing downgrade is one of a vampire's signature defences and werewolves have plenty of other advantages going for them.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's fair. And it does rather balance things out quite a bit where as oWoD didn't seem to care much about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1702-matty1love","name":"Matty1Love","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T07:40:22-07:00","id":122327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matty1Love</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=122275#post122275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's fair. And it does rather balance things out quite a bit where as oWoD didn't seem to care much about this.</div> </div> </div> </div> The old set of games had absolutely no consideration to each other for any kind of cross over potential. That didn't stop people from doing it, but the games sure as hell didn't support it. One of the reasons the new set of games are a lot more compatible. Quite frankly, werewolves having teeth and claws isn't what makes them scary to a vampire. It's the tactics a Werewolf can easily employ of hunting, harassing and harrying their target. The vampire against a smart Werewolf won't get a direct fight until they're weak on blood or daylight is approaching. Or the Werewolf is confident they'll win the direct conflict. But that assumes the vampire is isolated, out of their turf or similar. A realistically built vampire and Werewolf in a white room conflict should be a lot more even, because either of them being a push over doesn't make for interesting drama and hey, we're here to tell stories. ... I'd put money on the Werewolf though, but I'm biased <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T08:31:09-07:00","id":122348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=122182#post122182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never get this debate. The Uratha can simply shove a torch on the kindred's face for aggravated damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Detroit Rock City occasionally has a flashback scene for experimenting with shoving a garlic pizza in a vampire's face. With B&amp;S rules, that could even work!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T09:02:00-07:00","id":122375,"title":"","content":"Press any number of spirits into following the vampire to it's haven (there are several that would be ideal for the task), go back one morning with some cans of gas, have a nice BBQ.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T13:14:35-07:00","id":122610,"title":"","content":"Does vampire flesh count as human for the purposes of gaining Essence? What about in the eyes of the Oath?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T13:34:15-07:00","id":122631,"title":"","content":"I don't think so. To gain essence the flesh has to be fresh. That's not what I'd call what the Kindred have, blush of life or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T14:17:50-07:00","id":122661,"title":"","content":"Idunno, it definitely has something in it.<br /> Vampires can turn their vitae to essence.<br /> They have a soul, and vampires are, generally, fresh enough to keep moving.<br /> I suppose it depends whether you come at it from the idea that werewolves get essence from flesh because they are enacting their wolf resonance as predators, or whether it's because human flesh has some of their soul in it, and thus can be harvested for essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-30-2014, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T15:50:04-07:00","id":122724,"title":"","content":"Since this is the Gifts thread, and thus to do halfway between a teaser and an on-topic post for the current discussion of undead etc...<br /> <br /> So the old Death Gifts, right? I love the notion of a Gift that's symbolic of Death reflected through the spirit and Essence of a werewolf, but that wasn't really what Death did under the old rules. We had 2.5 Gifts in its list that were basically all about dealing with undead - The .5 is Death Sight, then there was Ghost Knife and Word of Quiet. That's an awful lot of focus for a game-line that doesn't even feature undead antagonists in its core book. The stuff for interacting with ghosts felt legit enough, but it was too much emphasis on the undead and not enough emphasis on the general symbolism of death. That conceptual ground ended up being covered by other, later Gifts like Bone, if I remember correctly.<br /> <br /> Now, Stew spoiled some of the Death Facets already in his Gifts article - Cold Embrace (Cunning), Bone Gnaw (Purity) and Eyes of the Dead (Wisdom). None of those are about directly fighting/interacting with undead (although Cold Embrace has some utility there). That leaves two Facets unspoiled. Well, <i>one</i> of those two Facets is all about dealing with undead. It rolls together stuff for the corporeal and incorporeal types under one roof and yes, a werewolf with that Facet is going to be pretty effective against vampires, among other things.<br /> <br /> So if you're in a Chronicle featuring undead and ghosts, or a crossover game where it's important for your werewolf to be able to combat those types of entities, everything you need is in the one Facet. That freed me up to have the other four Death Facets dealing with various interesting death-related elements, rather than the whole Death's Gift basically being Undead: The Fightening.<br /> <br /> Usual Disclaimer: This is as of first draft, second draft may change everything, do not quote me on this, I was never there, you didn't see nuffink guv.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T16:29:23-07:00","id":122750,"title":"","content":"Hey cool. Yeah the Death gifts bugged me, too.<br /> <br /> Nice to see that more abilities won't be hyper-focused, which was a real drag. Also nice to see the mentions of other splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-30-2014, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T00:29:06-07:00","id":125616,"title":"","content":"What I was worried about a bit when reading the gifts was, well, how universal will the theme of &quot;the wolf must hunt&quot; be?<br /> <br /> I do get that is the core of what is intended for the new werewolf iteration, but...<br /> <br /> To get straight to the point, I would definitely loose a ot of my interest in the Idigam chronicles if by rules and / or flavour it was ALL werewolves are supposed to do.<br /> <br /> Wolves are predators and all, well and good, but that is not the end to them, not even when you rephrase it to &quot;pack hunter&quot;.<br /> <br /> Will gifts and flavour also support the aspect of a wolf as protecting his territory and pack (and not just hunting what enters / crosses those)? Will it support the aspect of the survivor (above being really good at bringing down prey to eat), or the aspect of being a very social animal (caring for kin and family and such)?<br /> Will the less inherently &quot;wolfy&quot; werewolf themes of being a shaman or being in tune with nature still be something that gets some inherent value instead of just being about the hunt?<br /> <br /> I guess mostly the nature gifts dissatisfied me a bit in that they seemed a bit too directly focused on the hunt.<br /> What I mean is: there is a difference between a power being very good for hunting and being about the hunt.<br /> I think too much of the latter might run werewolf into a trap of crippling overspecialization.<br /> Theme IS important, but when it comes down to it, you need to face the reality that players will want different things (meaning, note very player in the group wanting the same), so it may really hamper the appeal if the game comes off as too much of just one thing.<br /> <br /> As a comparison, look at Vampire:<br /> It is often said it is a game of extreme intrigue and similar and, yes, that is supported aplenty by setting and rules.<br /> But it does have very distinct vampire archetypes, the Gagnrel being much more focused on the physical and the animal aspect, the Nosferatu being about fear, the Mekhet about the unseen and the shadow, the Daeva about seduction, etc.<br /> But even within one clan, there is enough room to be a very different beast (A Daeva with a very physical focus for example and less Majesty or similar).<br /> <br /> I admit, if auspices and tribes boil down to JUST being whether you are a &quot;social predator&quot;, a &quot;stalking hunter&quot; or a &quot;spirit chaser&quot;, it would be less fun for me at least...<br /> <br /> Of course, so far, we only have a glimpse of the gifts, but I really think that making the gifts more &quot;tools that work well for the hunt&quot; instead of &quot;tools just for hunting&quot; would not be bad.<br /> <br /> My own predilections aside, gifts should, I think, not run danger of being too narrow, we already had that before with some and I think it may be a turn off compared to more &quot;universal&quot; disciplines.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T00:45:01-07:00","id":125621,"title":"","content":"@Ray:<br /> <br /> Well, Nature gifts have been since their inception affinity to the Hunters in Darkness so that's probably a feature, not a bug. When it boils down to it, tho, werewolves are predators, with all the positive and negative connotation that this entails. Both the ones found in the animal kingdom, and how we refer to people who preys on other people for whichever reason.<br /> <br /> The hacker who exploits a cyber cafe and collects dozens of bank accounts information on a weekly basis. The corporate CEO spearheading one aggressive take over after another. The drug dealer. The scam artist. The undercover cop; the list can go on and on and on.<br /> <br /> Look at that, I just described an Iron Master Blessed Pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 05-05-2014, 03:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T01:31:09-07:00","id":125637,"title":"","content":"@Ephsy: As I said, I see the werewolf as more than JUST a hunter, yes, that theme is there and should be strong, but I fear that it will be a bit like that quintessential stereotype assessment &quot;all werewolves are like this&quot;.<br /> I see so much diversity in other game lines, amusingly quite a lot in Hunter (where one could argue that by the name it should be all about the hunt^^) where you can be about understanding the supernatural, or about being a &quot;holy warrior&quot;, or a monster understanding what it is like to be &quot;them&quot; (the lucifuge) or about beingmore of a monster than the monsters you hunt. You can be a protector of your lot or one to go out and seek the monsters...<br /> <br /> If werewolf ends up offering less thematic diversity, especially for the characters you play, then, well, then I am already out of the loop... ^^ ;<br /> <br /> I do fear it is already there anyway though, so, while I had a lot of hope for werewolf, I think I will not be buying the Idigam chronicle, not even for updated rules.<br /> Likely, I will rather stick to some chroniclers guide stuff and self made god machine updating.<br /> <br /> Nature gifts, yes, they had a theme that supported it, but they were more.<br /> <br /> Beast Speech and Beast Ride offered a lot of animal interaction powers, forest communion was great for both a hunt, but also looking for someone, guarding an area (the territory protection aspect was strong there) while plant growths and nature's vengeance also had lot of potential for more than hunting.<br /> <br /> I just think the new stuff feels a bit to focused...<br /> too much focus, as well as too little can be a bad thing...<br /> <br /> <br /> Ah, but, as I said, I think I will not be really in the target audience anymore... ^^;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T04:38:00-07:00","id":125714,"title":"","content":"Right, I'll address some points here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ray White</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=125616#post125616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Will gifts and flavour also support the aspect of a wolf as protecting his territory and pack (and not just hunting what enters / crosses those)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes; Warding Gifts have been given a serious kick to make them better on a pack and territory scale.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Will it support the aspect of the survivor (above being really good at bringing down prey to eat), or the aspect of being a very social animal (caring for kin and family and such)? </div> </div> </div>Yes, to my mind, although you'll need to define what you consider to be aspects of being a survivor a bit better for me to be able to say for sure, and yes, there are a number of social Facets. As I've said before (in this very thread, I think?) there are lots of Gifts that haven't been spoiled yet and some, like Inspiration and Dominance, fold into the social side.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Will the less inherently &quot;wolfy&quot; werewolf themes of being a shaman or being in tune with nature still be something that gets some inherent value instead of just being about the hunt? </div> </div> </div>Yes and yes, although being in tune with nature really does still focus around hunting given that, you know, wolves are hunters and this is a principle element of their natural existence. Hell, in shamanic terms there's stuff right there in the spoiled Facets - the 'riding' Facets for animals and machines - and Elemental's Gift should help cover some of that. In general, because I've drawn more on the symbolism of a Gift than the older style's random-knicknacks approach, the shamanistic element should be stronger across Gifts than before.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is often said it is a game of extreme intrigue and similar and, yes, that is supported aplenty by setting and rules.<br /> But it does have very distinct vampire archetypes, the Gagnrel being much more focused on the physical and the animal aspect, the Nosferatu being about fear, the Mekhet about the unseen and the shadow, the Daeva about seduction, etc.<br /> But even within one clan, there is enough room to be a very different beast (A Daeva with a very physical focus for example and less Majesty or similar). </div> </div> </div>So here's a thing.<br /> <br /> Vampire has 38 discreet supernatural powers in its Disciplines section.<br /> <br /> Werewolf has <i>110</i>.<br /> <br /> To a certain extent you will see individual Facets being more focused than Vampire powers because there are far more of them. If they weren't more focused then werewolves would have a supernatural power for every possibility under the sun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ray White</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=125637#post125637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast Speech and Beast Ride offered a lot of animal interaction powers,</div> </div> </div> </div>Beast Ride is right there in the new Facet list for Nature. Beast Speech exists somewhere else now - hell, might as well spoil it - it's no longer a 'Nature' power because it's far more core to the werewolf's essence and thus is available to all Uratha as a Wolf Gift Facet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> forest communion was great for both a hunt but also looking for someone, guarding an area (the territory protection aspect was strong there) </div> </div> </div>It also crossed over with a very similar Knowledge Gift in the old lists. These two Gifts have now been blended together and upgunned, and are now a Knowledge Facet that is more broadly applicable because the old Nature version couldn't be used in urban environments.<br /> <br /> In other words, the new take on this is more broadly useful than the old Gift was.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> while plant growths and nature's vengeance also had lot of potential for more than hunting. </div> </div> </div>Eh, plant growth is still sorta there in Call of the Wild, but I'm not massively keen for it to be a Nature Facet still. If you want that sort of thing, you can go looking for a nature spirit of the right type and get them to use their Influences to gain the effects you want; no need to take up a valuable Nature Facet slot with it. As for Nature's Vengeance, it's nasically an area debuff/attack; there are Facets that already cover the kind of penalties it throws around, and as I've said elsewhere (in this thread? can't remember) we've generally dropped the Killing You Gifts where a werewolf waggles his fingers and a target takes damage remotely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T07:17:24-07:00","id":125776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=125714#post125714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything you said makes me very, very happy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T08:16:09-07:00","id":125817,"title":"","content":"@Acrozatarim: First, I admit that what you say does raise my hopes a bit, at least from the mechanical point of view (which would be enough to buy the Idigam chronicles for me, since good mechanic compared to the rather messy core Forsaken ones would be worth buying even if I still had to fiddle around with the fluff).<br /> <br /> I still am a bit sceptical, but I do hope it is just that the first impression I got was skewed, especially if some of the stuff I thought replaced for a bit too hunting centred gifts is just elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Wolves are great at survival, they are spread through the entire northern hemisphere, they adapt well to different circumstances, be it different prey, scavenging or supplementing their diet with berries and such.<br /> They also can survive quite long on a single big meal, in short, they are really good all around predators while usually not being THE apex predator in their habitat and having to contend with very strong prey.<br /> <br /> I hope therefore to see some good gifts that emulate these qualities.<br /> I admit I am not sure if many of those were in the old werewolf core, but I knew Apocalypse had a few good fits.<br /> <br /> I would also like to see a bit more focus perhaps on especially Elodoth functions as intermediary (That is what I liked a bit more about the Philodox) between the packmates, and not just from the position of &quot;dominating&quot; others into behaving.<br /> <br /> About naure and hunting, I am more worried that at least mechanically, many gifts will be too much tilted towards working as a hunting tool rather than a general tool. Communing with nature to gather information, being able to use animals as more than just hunt support (though, that does seem to work from my reading).<br /> <br /> I think it would be kind of nifty if there was a bit of a divide betweent he more esoteric and shamanic powers and the ones that are more about, well, being a better hunter.<br /> I think there will surely be those players who want a lot of the shaman and others who want a lot of the hunter.<br /> Admittedly, sometimes I think it migh be worth thinking about making all of the shamanic stuff more a province of rites, but, I am digressing...<br /> <br /> <br /> Mainly, I hope for an overall breadth of choices what kind of werewolf to play.<br /> I think the theme of all wolves being hunters first and foremost instead of having more of a &quot;wolf that defends the territory&quot; &quot;unseen stalker&quot; &quot;social wolf&quot; and such does not sit too well with me...<br /> <br /> Maybe it is a bit like a typical dungeon fantasy where everyone is defined first and foremost as a treasure hunter, even when, while treasure hunting will be a major feature, many tyes of characters might be along mainly for quite different reasons.<br /> <br /> <br /> Lastly, I agree with not being too fond of the &quot;attack spell&quot; powers.<br /> It is exactly that kind of powers which can give werewolves more of a &quot;super&quot; or &quot;magic user&quot; who just happens to be furry feel which can be rather theme diluting.<br /> That WAS to my opinion one of the main faults of Apocalypse.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T09:11:18-07:00","id":125853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the theme of all wolves being hunters first and foremost instead of having more of a &quot;wolf that defends the territory&quot; &quot;unseen stalker&quot; &quot;social wolf&quot; and such does not sit too well with me... </div> </div> </div>I, for one, can play all of those with any Tribe/Auspice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T10:35:17-07:00","id":125941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=125853#post125853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I, for one, can play all of those with any Tribe/Auspice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think people are focusing too hard on &quot;preferred target&quot; versus the fact that it is not &quot;ignore everything if target exists.&quot; Just because I prefer cheeseburgers doesn't mean I am not going to eat the steak if the expiration date is coming up regardless of if a cheeseburger is also available.<br /> <br /> Same thing goes with the whole social, stalker, etc type of wolf. I can be an Elodoth Hunter in Darkness and still kick the ass of a Rahu Blood Talon if I build him right and he has the personality for it. It just means that when he isn't busy kicking the ass of upstart Uratha, he is busy fostering intra-pack negotiations, acting as a judge for a strange case involving a young uratha and a sheep, or even making a deal with a Changeling to provide them with protection in exchange for access to some Hedge roads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T12:17:36-07:00","id":126038,"title":"","content":"Crowning moment of awesome: my scrawny (Strength 2) ass Ithaeur Hunter in Darkness beating a PU 4 Rahu Blood Talon from the Lodge of Garm in a challenge, to the utter shock of his packmates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T13:15:05-07:00","id":126095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=126038#post126038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crowning moment of awesome: my scrawny (Strength 2) ass Ithaeur Hunter in Darkness beating a PU 4 Rahu Blood Talon from the Lodge of Garm in a challenge, to the utter shock of his packmates.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would have challenged him to a drinking contest, spiked his drink, and won through Cunning. I would then use it as an excuse to gain Cunning 3 or something from the Lunes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T13:36:30-07:00","id":126107,"title":"","content":"That wouldn't have been as awesome. Beat the player at his game is where it's at. The only tactic my PC did use, was &quot;No gifts, fight like a man.&quot; roughly, they were allowed to shapeshift and regenerate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T04:01:47-07:00","id":128127,"title":"","content":"I just read through the gifts, and I notice some gift facets give you good reason to NOT want a success or an exceptional success. For example, say you're running a chop shop. Unmake is a dream come true. But with an exceptional success, you can't reassemble any of those parts for a month! That's no good! In this case, you'd want just a normal success. Or with Garble, a dramatic failure gives the target a +1 on using technology. You have the really weird incentive to stack as many penalties on yourself as you can, then use it on your ally, and get a dramatic failure. They get a +1 on technology and you get a beat...when you really shouldn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T04:19:52-07:00","id":128138,"title":"","content":"Using a Gift carved into your soul to make auto repair a little faster is like using a gunshot to capture someone -- hilarious overkill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T05:07:48-07:00","id":128157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=128138#post128138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using a Gift carved into your soul to make auto repair a little faster is like using a gunshot to capture someone -- hilarious overkill.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the fact that it's hilarious makes it all the more enticing...and theme breaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T11:46:30-07:00","id":128416,"title":"","content":"I'm not seeing the case.<br /> <br /> &quot;This Gift could be really useful outside of it's intended application, but the exceptional success is too focused on its intended purpose to support the side application.&quot;<br /> <br /> You want to use the Gift to support your chop shop? Plenty enticing. And frankly, the benefits far outweigh the occasional exceptional success. But how is this theme breaking? The point of the Gift it to destroy. Trying to walk the edge of destroying just the right amount and sometimes destroying too much? Seems perfectly thematic for Forsaken.<br /> <br /> Trying to abuse Garble to get your friend a +1 bonus seems a waste. I'm sure there are far easier ways to give people +1 bonuses in the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T12:19:30-07:00","id":128443,"title":"","content":"This is where the storyteller needs to remember that he does, in some way, serve as karmic retribution. Or more specifically in the case of Werewolf, the storyteller serves as the spirits bowing to the Gift. S/he also needs to remember the functions of successes and failures.<br /> <br /> Let me expound on that second one before going back to the first. In writing, in storytelling, every conflict essentially has six answers, with four being more common than not. It breaks down into two aspects, the conflict resolution, and the resolution modifer. Putting it simpler, every conflict is essentially &quot;Does the character get what they want?&quot; to which the answer is either Yes or No, and each resolution(Yes/No) has some kind of catch or addition, manifested by the words But(when there is a small thing of benefit that comes out of failing), And(which means you magnify the benefit or the failing), and ....(which means you let it stand alone). Thus, every conflict has the potential for six resolutions: Yes, Yes But, Yes And, No, No But, and No And. As a general rule in normal storytelling, you avoid Yes resolutions until the end, and really avoid a Yes And unless you've really made the characters earn it. Otherwise, you drive the story predominantly with Yes But's, No's, and No And's, with the occassional No But as needed.<br /> <br /> In the World of Darkness, the four results kind of map nicely to the six, and even better these days where Disciplines, Gifts, Embeds and Exploits are written with the sense of making things happen. Exceptional Successes tend towards the Yes And answer, with the occasional simple Yes. Successes are traditionally simple Yes's, but in the case of disciplines, the attitude behind them is now leaning towards Yes But's. Failures are No's, and Dramatic Failures are No And's. No But's appear in various places here and there. At any given point in a game, a Storyteller needs to remember the spirit of what these mean, and enact accordingly.<br /> <br /> On Exceptional successes, it's a mixed bag, because spirits, while not bound to the letter of the rule, might be inclined to play that game simply because it's a good way of needling a werewolf, and what's more is that Yes But's drive the story better than Yes's or Yes And's...but the idea is that you earned an Exceptional Success. It comes to the moment of the story to decide if it's more appropriate to ruin a place regardless of what you want, or to give the player what they want out of the response.<br /> <br /> Failures I'm a little more hardline on, and I think people should be too. Failures means <i>things don't work out</i>. The general writing is geared towards situations where it would work against you-you aim to harm an enemy and instead help them. If a player is out to exploit that idea, then it's time to ignore the rules(maybe, read on), and enact the spirit of it. In game, a failure means that you haven't harnessed the respect of the spirits enacting the gift, so <i>of course they are going to fuck with you</i>. To do it deliberately? That invites Renown loss and probably a lot of shit, because now you are shitting on the spirits as well as your own fearsome reputation. Either way, a Failure is to be punished.<br /> <br /> The exception is treating an abuse like that as a Yes But....with probably a inevitable lead into a No or No And. Okay, you got a bonus to your car repair. The car runs better. Later when driving, you get caught up in the feel, and you get pulled over, and oh shit, the guy who pulled you over? Touched in just a way that you can't easily get him to supernaturally let it go, and probably isn't inclined to letting you go otherwise. You want out of it, it's gonna be a little messy.<br /> <br /> Maintain the spirit of the effects in all things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T13:28:00-07:00","id":128479,"title":"","content":"@ Arc:<br /> <br /> The thing with Gift is that they're usually written in the werewolf. Unless the Gift states specifically you're interacting with some spirit and having them do your job for you, that's not the case. What you're describing are Rites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T13:40:31-07:00","id":128488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=128479#post128479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@ Arc:<br /> <br /> The thing with Gift is that they're usually written in the werewolf. Unless the Gift states specifically you're interacting with some spirit and having them do your job for you, that's not the case. What you're describing are Rites.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm not.<br /> <br /> I don't have it on me right now(hooray for dying computers!), but I think a lot of us are familiar with the &quot;Gifts are all about dominance&quot; essay. In that, one of the writers for Lore of the Forsaken explains the way it all works-Gifts basically work because a werewolf asserts dominance over the local spirits(both because they've earned the mark via Gifts and their Renown), and because the show of dominance asserts a reason to respect the werewolf via the dicepool). A werewolf isn't making the fire jump onto the guy, the werewolf is spiritually snarling at the world and the fire falls in line. The difference between Gifts and Rites is that Gifts are the metaphysical equivalent of a bark of command, where as a Rite is a werewolf shouting a list of orders at spirits.<br /> <br /> Gifts are all about dominance. That idea only works if you are dominating someone in the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T13:55:35-07:00","id":128497,"title":"","content":"<b>Lore of the Forsaken</b> goes and explicitly says that Gifts are the Werewolf's to use like Numina. What you're describing is having a spirit using it's influence on your behalf. That's a rite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T14:07:58-07:00","id":128509,"title":"","content":"We're getting caught up on in-game metaphysical semantics.<br /> <br /> The point still stands: Failures are failures. Adjust power enactment accordingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T14:52:20-07:00","id":128533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=128416#post128416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not seeing the case.<br /> <br /> &quot;This Gift could be really useful outside of it's intended application, but the exceptional success is too focused on its intended purpose to support the side application.&quot;<br /> <br /> You want to use the Gift to support your chop shop? Plenty enticing. And frankly, the benefits far outweigh the occasional exceptional success. But how is this theme breaking? The point of the Gift it to destroy. Trying to walk the edge of destroying just the right amount and sometimes destroying too much? Seems perfectly thematic for Forsaken.<br /> <br /> Trying to abuse Garble to get your friend a +1 bonus seems a waste. I'm sure there are far easier ways to give people +1 bonuses in the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean it's theme breaking to try and use it for a chop shop to begin with. The Gift is designed to mimic horror movie tropes, like unmanned cars trying to run someone over and cell phones never working.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T15:29:01-07:00","id":128560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=128533#post128533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I mean it's theme breaking to try and use it for a chop shop to begin with. The Gift is designed to mimic horror movie tropes, like unmanned cars trying to run someone over and cell phones never working.</div> </div> </div> </div> Honestly, I don't find a blue collar Werewolf using his Luna-given Gifts to make his job in the repair shop a little easier to be at all theme breaking for Werewolf. Maybe it's just me, but I see Werewolf as the quintessential Everyman game. The game where you have to fight tooth and nail every day for the right to carve out a little piece of the world to call your own, against odds you have no hope of ever really beating, but between you and your friends you'll give it a hell of a shot. And at the end of that day, you get the one thing no one else in the World of Darkness ever gets - a precious few moments of peace where you can just kick your feet up, crack open a beer, and shoot the shit with your pack. And if you'd rather use your spirit powers to make the TV turn itself on rather than bother trying to find the remote, I'd say you damn well earned that right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T15:33:00-07:00","id":128568,"title":"","content":"If anything, werewolves need some boosting away from the everyman image.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T16:57:08-07:00","id":128621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=128568#post128568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If anything, werewolves need some boosting away from the everyman image.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd say that's a matter of play style. I like that aspect as a contrast to the jaded immortals and alien monsters of the other lines. Admittedly, it does run up against Hunter's themes a bit. But Werewolf does that a lot anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T23:39:57-07:00","id":128781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=128533#post128533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean it's theme breaking to try and use it for a chop shop to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cunning is a Renown category for a reason. Being creative with your powers is not against the themes of the game.<br /> <br /> Yes, the primary focus of the Gift is not making running a chop shop easier. But the fact that a character could do that doesn't damage the themes involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T00:31:25-07:00","id":128795,"title":"","content":"Lore of the Forsaken also talks that gifts become part of the Uratha and they don't have a lot of reasons to not use them, other than time or cost issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T08:33:10-07:00","id":238203,"title":"","content":"Just thought I'd let everyone know that I'm rereading through this thread as I hammer my final draft submission of Gifts into shape <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T15:29:35-07:00","id":238607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=238203#post238203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just thought I'd let everyone know that I'm rereading through this thread as I hammer my final draft submission of Gifts into shape <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Can we get a small preview of any Gift? Elemental, weather, rage, wolf gifts any one will do. The book is taking too long to come out!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T15:40:02-07:00","id":238625,"title":"","content":"If enough people were interested, I might be able to persuade Stew to let me preview one <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T15:44:01-07:00","id":238628,"title":"","content":"Call me greatly interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T16:01:35-07:00","id":238643,"title":"","content":"Weather would be cool, but it might be nice to see another of the ones that scales in power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T17:39:51-07:00","id":238706,"title":"","content":"Hell yeah I'm interested! Actually, I'd dig seeing how the Strength or Rage gifts play out. Not only because I'm thinking of combat ability, but the hilarity of Cunning Strength and Wise Rage makes me chuckle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T19:12:35-07:00","id":238768,"title":"","content":"Inspiration would be nice to sneak a peek at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T22:41:48-07:00","id":238870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=238625#post238625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If enough people were interested, I might be able to persuade Stew to let me preview one <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm interested. In Rage specifically. And also jealous of the Mage fans' recent spell spoilers","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T00:57:46-07:00","id":238935,"title":"","content":"Hell yes. I'd say Gibbous, but Inspiration works too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T04:19:20-07:00","id":239018,"title":"","content":"Ok, I have the go-ahead to give you some more info about a few Gifts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Note that these may change between now and final print - not only am I still putting the finishing touches to my second draft but obviously play-testing feedback, editing etc may alter them further.<br /> <br /> For starters, let's go with a brief outline of the Gift of Rage.<br /> <br /> For <b>Cunning</b>, we have <b>Incite Rage</b>. This lets you try and goad a target into Wasu-Im, the 'soft' Rage. It's a Contested dice pool, and the target has to be able to hear you mocking or challenging them. But wait, what if you target someone who is not a werewolf? Well, in that case success applies the Berserk Condition to them. The Condition does what it says on the tin - sends them into a berserk rage.<br /> <br /> Are you a werewolf with <b>Glory?</b> Then try <b>Berserker's Might</b>, useable in Dalu and Gauru. It's a reflexive action that, once per turn, lets you either reduce damage from an attack by your Glory dots or lets you immediately heal a physical Tilt. Arm Wrack? Gone! Persistent Arm Wrack? Also gone! I mean, werewolves can heal severed limbs etc anyway, but this lets you do it in a trice. Oh, and the damage reduction doesn't care what kind of damage it is, whether bashing, lethal or aggravated.<br /> <br /> For the <b>Honor</b>able werewolf, <b>Perfected Rage</b> is nice and straightforward. Add your Honor to the number of turns you can maintain Gauru for. Be a regenerating killing machine for longer.<br /> <br /> <b>Purity</b> gets right to the essence of what Rage is all about with <b>Slaughterer</b>. You can only use Slaughterer in Gauru when you hit with a Brawl attack, whereupon you add your Purity dots to the damage inflicted.<br /> <br /> And finally, for <b>Wisdom</b>, <b>Raging Lunacy</b> lets you choose to apply the Berserk Condition on people affected by your Lunacy instead of the usual Lunacy Conditions.<br /> <br /> Something else to note; several Facets, like both Berserker's Might and Slaughterer, get activated <i>for free</i> and used instinctively when you enter full-bore Death Rage. Shoving an enemy werewolf into <i>Basu-Im</i> can actually make them even scarier...<br /> <br /> So for the other Gifts I'll reveal the contents of, I'm currently thinking Strength, Inspiration and then one of the three Moon Gifts we haven't revealed as yet. Cahalith? Rahu? Ithaeur?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T05:44:12-07:00","id":239048,"title":"","content":"Oooooohh...<br /> <br /> Cahalith. Go on. This is pure gold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T05:47:29-07:00","id":239050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=239018#post239018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For <b>Cunning</b>, we have <b>Incite Rage</b>. This lets you try and goad a target into Wasu-Im, the 'soft' Rage. It's a Contested dice pool, and the target has to be able to hear you mocking or challenging them. But wait, what if you target someone who is not a werewolf? Well, in that case success applies the Berserk Condition to them. The Condition does what it says on the tin - sends them into a berserk rage.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Is 2nd edition going to follow the same rule 1st has in that anything that can cause Rage in a Werewolf can cause Frenzy in a Vampire and visa versa? Or is that left to individual STs like with a lot of the old crossover stuff? Though to me, it makes even MORE sense now, given the parallels between beast/hunter now.<br /> <br /> I like the split of the gift facets there, at any rate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T07:08:33-07:00","id":239092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=239050#post239050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is 2nd edition going to follow the same rule 1st has in that anything that can cause Rage in a Werewolf can cause Frenzy in a Vampire and visa versa? Or is that left to individual STs like with a lot of the old crossover stuff? Though to me, it makes even MORE sense now, given the parallels between beast/hunter now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure yet, I'm still nailing down the text of the Berserk Condition.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, so, the Gift of Inspiration next.<br /> <br /> For <b>Cunning</b> you have <b>Lunatic Inspiration</b>. Touch a human or Wolf-Blooded and succeed at the contested roll, and you slap the Inspiration and Madness Conditions on them. The target is driven by the moon-mad inspiration that strikes him each night in his dreams, driven to create a work of art from the revelations he is receiving. The Inspiration Condition renews each day. If he doesn't manage it by the next full moon, the Inspiration stops coming - and the Madness becomes persistent.<br /> <br /> For <b>Glory</b> it's <b>Fearless Hunter</b>. Not only does the Uratha add her Glory to her resistance and contested dice pools against fear and mind-influencing effects, but she leads by example - if you pass a contested roll against such an effect, you can spend Essence so that your packmates who fail actually succeed instead.<br /> <br /> When it comes to <b>Honor</b>, Inspiration provides you with <b>Pack Triumphs Together</b>. You can use this at the beginning of a combat by spending Essence depending on how many packmates you're affecting. Once Initiative is rolled, all affected packmates can move up to the highest Initiative rolled by any packmate. Out of combat it can be used to add 8-again to teamwork actions.<br /> <br /> The <b>Purity</b> Facet is <b>Unity</b>. Is one of your pack being targeted by a social manoeuver? Step in with Unity and add your Purity to the number of Doors the social manoeuver has to break through for it to be successful.<br /> <br /> Finally, the <b>Wisdom</b> of Inspiration is <b>Still Small Voice</b>. This contested roll lets you drag werewolves who are in <i>Wasu-Im</i>, the 'soft' Rage, out of their growing fury and return them to calm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T09:01:12-07:00","id":239189,"title":"","content":"Just take my money now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T10:18:24-07:00","id":239306,"title":"","content":"Wow, Still Small Voice may prove to be a Gift tax. I'm sure having a hard time picturing a pack not pressuring at least one member to learn it. Probably two in case the pack's primary user Death Rages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T10:20:34-07:00","id":239308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=239306#post239306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, Still Small Voice may prove to be a Gift tax. I'm sure having a hard time picturing a pack not pressuring at least one member to learn it. Probably two in case the pack's primary user Death Rages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can sort of see this happening, but with the changes in death rage, I think it is far less mandatory. Couple that with the fact that it is a Wisdom facet makes it a bit harder for multiple members to pick up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T10:40:33-07:00","id":239319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=239306#post239306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, Still Small Voice may prove to be a Gift tax. I'm sure having a hard time picturing a pack not pressuring at least one member to learn it. Probably two in case the pack's primary user Death Rages.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Death Rage rules have been worked on; the Chain Rage Rite and Still Small Voice are not the only ways to prevent someone in Soft Rage entering full Death Rage when their time is up. They do, obviously make it safer as you're putting up additional safety nets to catch your ragers before they go full-bore berserker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T11:37:59-07:00","id":239378,"title":"","content":"Well, now that I've sent off my final draft for Gifts, I'm now second-guessing myself about the power levels, the overlap between certain Facets, the replacement Nature Glory Facet...<br /> <br /> To take my mind off that, what would people like to see as the last Shadow Gift that I spoil? Strength? Elemental? Something else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T11:38:47-07:00","id":239380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=239319#post239319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Death Rage rules have been worked on; the Chain Rage Rite and Still Small Voice are not the only ways to prevent someone in Soft Rage entering full Death Rage when their time is up. They do, obviously make it safer as you're putting up additional safety nets to catch your ragers before they go full-bore berserker.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, ok. As long as there are multiple ways to end Wasu-Im without going to Basu-Im, I'm not worried.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T11:50:39-07:00","id":239383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=239092#post239092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, the <b>Wisdom</b> of Inspiration is <b>Still Small Voice</b>. This contested roll lets you drag werewolves who are in <i>Wasu-Im</i>, the 'soft' Rage, out of their growing fury and return them to calm.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems just slightly too specific to the werewolf template, any chance of seeing it broadened to be a &quot;Calm The Fuck Down&quot; button? Like Incite Rage, but the other direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T12:18:14-07:00","id":239396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=239378#post239378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, now that I've sent off my final draft for Gifts, I'm now second-guessing myself about the power levels, the overlap between certain Facets, the replacement Nature Glory Facet...<br /> <br /> To take my mind off that, what would people like to see as the last Shadow Gift that I spoil? Strength? Elemental? Something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Strength please. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It is the most core to the Werewolf idea in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T12:31:16-07:00","id":239461,"title":"","content":"Weather, if there is one. Otherwise Elemental.<br /> <br /> I don't see why everyone should have a supernatural ability to calm down other werewolves, I like the facet as is. You could probably expand it to try calming down frenzying other things, or berserked wolf-blooded and humans.<br /> <br /> I really like Raging Lunacy and Lunatic Inspiration. Though I'm hoping it says non-Werewolf, not limiting it to just humans and wolf blooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-24-2014, 09:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T13:39:30-07:00","id":239533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=239378#post239378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, now that I've sent off my final draft for Gifts, I'm now second-guessing myself about the power levels, the overlap between certain Facets, the replacement Nature Glory Facet...</div> </div> </div> </div>If it turns out to be horrendously overpowered, isn't there a type of feedback stage after the POD is usually released? I know we do this now for typos and bugs, but if there is significant outcry, who knows?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=239378#post239378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To take my mind off that, what would people like to see as the last Shadow Gift that I spoil? Strength? Elemental? Something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>I dare to be different than the 2 who posted before me and say Stealth. Otherwise I will vote for Elemental<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-