arim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=239378#post239378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, now that I've sent off my final draft for Gifts, I'm now second-guessing myself about the power levels, the overlap between certain Facets, the replacement Nature Glory Facet...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well if something does not work as intended you can always fix it after the pdf comes out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=239378#post239378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To take my mind off that, what would people like to see as the last Shadow Gift that I spoil? Strength? Elemental? Something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Strength and Weather get my vote. But I'll be happy with any gift. Thanks for the spoilers!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T17:04:20-07:00","id":239679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=239378#post239378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, now that I've sent off my final draft for Gifts, I'm now second-guessing myself about the power levels, the overlap between certain Facets, the replacement Nature Glory Facet...</div> </div> </div> </div>It looks fine. I would have suggested something, but everything I came up with seemed (to me) to fit snugly under the Elemental Glory Facet. :-/<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T17:35:21-07:00","id":239700,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, I'll go with Elemental!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T18:13:56-07:00","id":239757,"title":"","content":"Strength Gift! Also: all of these Gifts are super-rad. I'm slavering for <b>Werewolf: The Forsaken - Second Edition</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T18:40:52-07:00","id":239780,"title":"","content":"Another for Strength! I'm planning on playing a Rahu in an upcoming chronicle when 2nd edition drops, and rage already has me heavily reconsidering not dumping all of my renown into purity XD. That said, even with the small sampling of gifts I've seen so far, that is still a really hard decision. I'm super stoked for this edition because all of the gifts and facets create a multitude of choices, I can see many, many, many different ways to build a starting character, even if it has the same tribe and auspice that all play very differently, and that's with just four shadow gifts presented!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T20:18:37-07:00","id":239842,"title":"","content":"Another for the pile of Elemental stuff, mostly for reasons of wanting to see what's become of the old list's &quot;you can adapt these Gifts to any of the four classical elements&quot; aspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T20:21:42-07:00","id":239843,"title":"","content":"I vote Weather, then Elemental. I run nice, ice bound game on North Sweden, under watchful eye of Winter Wolf - would love to see what powers can he bestow on PCs. Or throw against them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T23:26:07-07:00","id":239957,"title":"","content":"There's been all this talk about the Elemental Gifts, so of course I need to push that button.<br /> <br /> I am a well trained monkey!<br /> <br /> And after that, The Cahalith Moon Gifts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-25-2014, 02:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T00:44:12-07:00","id":239996,"title":"","content":"I'm not normally a fan of Elemental Gifts, but Satchel sold me. I am curious to see how translating to different elements will be handled. Also, any chance of a Wolf Gift teaser? I don't want to get greedy, but they're really the Gifts I'm most interested in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T02:51:34-07:00","id":240064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=239957#post239957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's been all this talk about the Elemental Gifts, so of course I need to push that button.<br /> <br /> I am a well trained monkey!<br /> <br /> And after that, The Cahalith Moon Gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>*hands you a piece of banana* Good monkey. :-)<br /> <br /> Although honestly, all of the Gifts kick ass. Everyone should buy Chris drinks for what he did there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T03:20:07-07:00","id":240080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Red 9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=239383#post239383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This seems just slightly too specific to the werewolf template, any chance of seeing it broadened to be a &quot;Calm The Fuck Down&quot; button? Like Incite Rage, but the other direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not, if only for simplicity's sake and saving word count. Individual Storytellers can rule for their games as they desire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=239461#post239461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really like Raging Lunacy and Lunatic Inspiration. Though I'm hoping it says non-Werewolf, not limiting it to just humans and wolf blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunatic Inspiration currently says humans and Wolf-Blooded. Nothing will break if you decide that human includes mages, changelings etc. It shouldn't include vampires or other undead though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=239533#post239533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it turns out to be horrendously overpowered, isn't there a type of feedback stage after the POD is usually released? I know we do this now for typos and bugs, but if there is significant outcry, who knows?</div> </div> </div> </div>That won't be up to me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Anyway, I'm not expecting 'significant outcry', it's just that bit where you have to let go of your creation and have no more time to tweak or adjust, and you start to second-guess yourself... did I do that Facet right? Will people like this Facet? Is it ok that, out of 125 individual powers, these four Facets all cover somewhat similar territory in different ways? etc etc.<br /> <br /> Of course, if anything <i>does</i> turn out to be totally borked and somehow doesn't get picked up in playtesting etc, then I'm sure we'll try and get it sorted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T03:43:14-07:00","id":240095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=239679#post239679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It looks fine. I would have suggested something, but everything I came up with seemed (to me) to fit snugly under the Elemental Glory Facet. :-/</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I had the same problem <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Speaking of which, it looks like Elemental has won out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So, the <b>Gift of the Elementals</b><br /> <br /> As we've said several times, I did something a bit experimental with this Gift. First up was the way the old Elemental Gift did the thing where it had a set element for each step, but tucked away in the blurb at the beginning that you could legitimately come up with separate Elemental lists for each one. I specifically didn't want to do another Gift list where the first dot was Water, the second dot Earth, etc.<br /> <br /> Secondly, back when we were discussing the new Gifts system and how we wanted to do it, I mooted to Stew the idea of Gifts that would give Influence dots to werewolves. In the final drafts I've submitted, werewolves have several ways of accessing Influences - certain Rites, Fetishes, and Talens. Also, the Gift of the Elementals.<br /> <br /> Four of the Elemental Facets give Influence. <b>Cunning's</b> Facet is <b>Breath of Air; Honor</b> is <b>Flesh of Earth; Purity</b> offers <b>Tongue of Flame</b> and <b>Wisdom</b> is the <b>Heart of Water</b>. Each of these gives the werewolf dots in Influence for the relevant element equal to her dots in the corresponding Renown. An Uratha with Purity 3 and Tongue of Flame has Influence (Fire) 3. Each also specifies the dice pool that the werewolf uses for that Influence in place of the usual Power + Finesse; Heart of Water is Manipulation + Occult + Wisdom, for example.<br /> <br /> Then there;s the <b>Glory</b> Facet, <b>Catastrophe</b>.<br /> <br /> Catastrophe doesn't do a lot by itself; if you just acquired Catastrophe and none of the other Facets from this Gift, then you're immune to the Catastrophe-enhanced Influences of another werewolf but that's all. However, you can use Catastrophe whenever you use one of the other four Facets' Influences. Catastrophe turns the Influence use into an extended action and eats up a huge amount of Essence; you'll actually need to be a fairly high Primal Urge to get the higher levels of use out of it. However, its effect is to take the Influence you're using and make it affect an area of miles in radius equal to your Glory Renown.<br /> <br /> This, obviously, can be rather devastating. Even just Strengthen, the first dot of Influence, can cause fires across the area to blaze out of control or winds to whip up into a howling gale. Manipulating Earth lets you tear avalanches down from the mountains. Create Water for mass flooding. Etc etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, last of all for my spoilers for now, I'll be giving the full text of a Moon Gift. Looks like Cahalith is winning the push at the moment, but I'll leave it a bit longer to see if anyone else wants to pitch in with their opinion <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"h