age. Followed by the option to reflexively invalidate Wolfie's attack, five times. Vampires are capable of combat shenanigans too you know <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But now we're way off topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh.<br /> <br /> I'm actually a little sad that that was possible. Gonna have to pay closer attention to my players' choices from here on out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T09:52:42-07:00","id":243220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=243203#post243203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lord no. Barring the fact that he was a PC (and you don't invoke D&amp;D against PCs), the vampire could still have cleanly eviscerated Mr. Wolfie. Massive Defense + Thurst + Physical Intensity + Magicy Rapier = ~30 dice, predefense, of Aggravated Damage. Followed by the option to reflexively invalidate Wolfie's attack, five times. Vampires are capable of combat shenanigans too you know <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>All of that is meaningless if they slap Submissive on the vamp and then proceed with Down &amp; Dirty thanks to Gauru.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 08-28-2014, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T09:55:10-07:00","id":243223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=243214#post243214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh.<br /> <br /> I'm actually a little sad that that was possible. Gonna have to pay closer attention to my players' choices from here on out.</div> </div> </div> </div>WoD is a sandbox, exploitation comes with the territory. I always make a point of double-checking character sheets to make sure no one character grossly outstrips others. Though, in this particular PCs case, him being much more potent than the others was kinda the point (he played closer to an antagonist than a hero).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T10:16:15-07:00","id":243255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=243220#post243220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of that is meaningless if the slap Submissive on the vamp and then proceed with Down &amp; Dirty thanks to Gauru.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is getting worryingly close to White Room. You mention submissive, I add competitive, you say Gauru, I say Frenzy, it goes on forever. There is always a theoretical way to one-up the opposition.<br /> <br /> Final word, because this is way off topic from Gifts, no single power should be used to shut down and murder a PC. Even if its written that way, the Storyteller just shouldn't do it, nor should he allow a potentially awesome scene to be handwaved away. Werewolves don't automatically dominate every fight just because they are wolves (Can you imagine? It'd be so boring...), there's always someone who is better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 08-28-2014, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T10:16:25-07:00","id":243256,"title":"","content":"Its not really broken, and &quot;easily&quot; accessible to anyone else in the system. A character that invests in combat powers, skills, and fighting styles is going to a beast if done properly. Vampires are supernatural monsters just as Werewolves are. Pulling out crazy numbers comes with the territory when you have someone focusing on a field.<br /> <br /> A Vampire with Celerity and Thrust is a hilarious combo, and I'm glad you pointed it out. &gt;:3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T10:44:02-07:00","id":243277,"title":"","content":"Another thing I continue to find funny. People worried about Shadow Gifts being removed from the Dot System and &quot;normalized&quot; on the same wavelength would weaken them. I figure the teasers have calmed that talk down. XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T10:51:21-07:00","id":243279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=243085#post243085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Despite being the one that suggested the Strength and Rage gift teasers I wonder how the social side of things fall for Uratha now. I figure the Gift of Dominance is the go-to thing, and wonder if the 1e restriction of only working on mortals, wolf-blooded, and werewolves is still there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember mentioning this quite a while back; the Gift of Dominance no longer has its restriction on targets, although one of the Facets is essentially restricted because it alters the effect of Lunacy (which won't affect werewolves, other supernatural beings etc).<br /> <br /> The old Gift of Dominance was largely 'give an order that must be obeyed' with increasing effect as the dots rose. The new one doesn't work really work like that - if nothing else, it's five individual powers rather than the old one's effective 3 powers. More than that, though, I looked towards making several of the Dominance Facets interface with the social manouever system, where the Vampire powers tend to do an end-run round them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T10:58:29-07:00","id":243285,"title":"","content":"That's perfect for me. My social-heavy Iron Master Irraka always went with the manipulative shadowy figure way of social, and something that actually plays into the social system would go well with that.<br /> <br /> Vampire tends to bash social over the head and get to the results. Which, being the Social Splat, I figured is the main idea.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T11:29:35-07:00","id":243300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=243279#post243279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I remember mentioning this quite a while back; the Gift of Dominance no longer has its restriction on targets, although one of the Facets is essentially restricted because it alters the effect of Lunacy (which won't affect werewolves, other supernatural beings etc).<br /> <br /> The old Gift of Dominance was largely 'give an order that must be obeyed' with increasing effect as the dots rose. The new one doesn't work really work like that - if nothing else, it's five individual powers rather than the old one's effective 3 powers. More than that, though, I looked towards making several of the Dominance Facets interface with the social manouever system, where the Vampire powers tend to do an end-run round them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do we have a fixed Primal Howl? aka. &quot;Feel Lunacy, Mage.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T12:00:48-07:00","id":243316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=243300#post243300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do we have a fixed Primal Howl? aka. &quot;Feel Lunacy, Mage.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There are currently no Facets that apply Lunacy to beings that would not normally suffer it.<br /> <br /> That said, it's the kind of thing I'd put in the theoretical Gift of Fear/Terror that I have on my list of Gifts I Want To Do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T12:41:41-07:00","id":243338,"title":"","content":"Oh do those for bale hounds. Hell yes.<br /> <br /> Edit: you actually could do facets for every type of bale hound. That'd make a rad challenge!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":1939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","user":"Lyrics Of War","date":". 08-28-2014, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T14:05:48-07:00","id":243390,"title":"","content":"Tainted moon gifts from the Iduth-Su, the Flayed Lunes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T14:59:44-07:00","id":243440,"title":"","content":"Terror or Fear is one of the ones I'd like to do as a general Shadow Gift, along with Madness, Sea, Sun, City Mk II, probably a general 'Emotion' one... Hell, I could write Gifts all day <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T15:06:01-07:00","id":243444,"title":"","content":"Hell, just having a Gift of the Sun would be interesting. Helios having heavy dislike of his sister's kids is talked about in a few places. So I imagine getting his Helions to grant you a taste of that power would be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T15:15:23-07:00","id":243453,"title":"","content":"Would they be as crazy as lunes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T17:48:49-07:00","id":243503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=243440#post243440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Terror or Fear is one of the ones I'd like to do as a general Shadow Gift, along with Madness, Sea, Sun, City Mk II, probably a general 'Emotion' one... Hell, I could write Gifts all day <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I would love to see a City Gift under the new system. Also, a redo of stuff from <b>The Rage</b> that aren't making it in the new core (cleaned up Alpha's Howl would be good, although there are other Gifts in there that I really like - such as most of the Stalking Gifts). And by all means, write Gifts all day, because they're freaking awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T18:11:03-07:00","id":243511,"title":"","content":"One of the complaints I've heard about Lodges is that people don't like them because they don't offer new gift sets. The specific comparisons I heard were usually to Mage's legacies and Vampire's bloodlines (not all of which offered their own disciplines, of course). Obviously overloading on gifts can be seen as a problem, but they're just...kinda fun. And with the limitations (auspice only gifts are auspice only, I think, as opposed to things anyone not of that auspice can learn but at a higher cost) the more options the better.<br /> <br /> Plus considering how cool the ones we've seen are other more outre gifts would just be mindblowing, I'm sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T21:35:06-07:00","id":243625,"title":"","content":"Funny, I always wished vampire bloodlines were more like werewolf lodges, and as of strix chronicles I got my wish. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T04:19:42-07:00","id":246073,"title":"","content":"I'd be very wary of Lodges being a major soruce of new Gifts - among other things, I'd rather pitch widely available Shadow Gifts rather than really specialised, really restricted ones. I can see a few Lodges having unusual Gift access but I think it's better if Lodges generally give other special capabiltiies.<br /> <br /> I mean, back in 1e, I wrote up a regional Lodge of the Stannary for a Cornwall game I ran, and created a Stannary Gift for them, but it's basically a 'Gift of Metal' and, were I to write it again, I'd just do it as a generally available Shadow Gift of Metal; the bits of the Gift that were more to do with underground stuff I'd split out into a separate Gift of Caverns or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T04:28:08-07:00","id":246076,"title":"","content":"Any chance of a glance at the Gifts of hunting?<br /> <br /> Happy Monday!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T05:27:30-07:00","id":246089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=246073#post246073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be very wary of Lodges being a major soruce of new Gifts - among other things, I'd rather pitch widely available Shadow Gifts rather than really specialised, really restricted ones. I can see a few Lodges having unusual Gift access but I think it's better if Lodges generally give other special capabiltiies.<br /> <br /> I mean, back in 1e, I wrote up a regional Lodge of the Stannary for a Cornwall game I ran, and created a Stannary Gift for them, but it's basically a 'Gift of Metal' and, were I to write it again, I'd just do it as a generally available Shadow Gift of Metal; the bits of the Gift that were more to do with underground stuff I'd split out into a separate Gift of Caverns or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with Acrozatarim. Some Lodges may have secret Gifts, but they should be the exception, not the norm.<br /> <br /> Lodges should offer something, but I don't think that something should always be a new Gift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T05:43:15-07:00","id":246093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hoodedclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=246076#post246076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any chance of a glance at the Gifts of hunting?<br /> <br /> Happy Monday!</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you want to have exceptionally honed senses, or to scent the prey's trail through impossible spoor? Do you desire to speak with beasts, to be a tireless hunter who cares nothing for food or weariness on the Siskur-Dah, who leaves the foe cowed just by knowing they are the subject of the Sacred Hunt?<br /> <br /> That's the Gift of Hunting.<br /> <br /> Various Facets are being shuffled around since we added the new Gift of the Pack to the Wolf Gifts, making it three Wolf Gifts in total in the corebook.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T06:02:28-07:00","id":246100,"title":"","content":"You, sir (/madam), are a gent (/lady).<br /> <br /> Gift of the Pack? Wow. Appropriating the themes deeper into the hardware, it seems. Very nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T06:36:26-07:00","id":246116,"title":"","content":"Any chance for a rough guideline for comming up with our own gifts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3301-the-inevitable","name":"The Inevitable","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T07:03:58-07:00","id":246124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Inevitable</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=246116#post246116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any chance for a rough guideline for comming up with our own gifts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Stew has suggested that we might do a blog post about designing Gifts after the book has been released.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T07:32:28-07:00","id":246134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=246124#post246124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stew has suggested that we might do a blog post about designing Gifts <b>after the book has been released</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book will be released this month, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T08:01:12-07:00","id":246146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackheartz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=246134#post246134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The book will be released this month, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've done my writing bit and dunno what the production schedule is for the rest of the process, so you'd have to check with Stew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T09:02:00-07:00","id":247895,"title":"","content":"*prays to the development gods*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3777-the-scorpion","name":"The Scorpion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T01:59:19-07:00","id":250599,"title":"","content":"So... Stealth Gifts (provided this is still on-going)... Do we still have a Feet of Mist-like ability that lets us mask our scent?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","name":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T05:01:44-07:00","id":250661,"title":"","content":"Feet of Mist is now an Evasion Facet.<br /> <br /> You know before, where Feet of Mist gave a minute penalty to people tracking you unless you spent Willpower, when it gave a slightly less minute penalty?<br /> <br /> The new Feet of Mist is, er, quite a bit better than that. I'll just spoil the first line of it: &quot;For the duration of the Facet, all attempts to track or locate the Uratha fail.&quot;<br /> <br /> Obviously there's more to the Facet than that, since we cover eg what happens in a Clash of Wills against a supernatural power that's tracking the Uratha (suffice to say that a Clash of Wills takes place but Feet of Mist is rather likely to win out).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T08:39:04-07:00","id":250783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=250661#post250661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feet of Mist is now an Evasion Facet.<br /> <br /> You know before, where Feet of Mist gave a minute penalty to people tracking you unless you spent Willpower, when it gave a slightly less minute penalty?<br /> <br /> The new Feet of Mist is, er, quite a bit better than that. I'll just spoil the first line of it: &quot;For the duration of the Facet, all attempts to track or locate the Uratha fail.&quot;<br /> <br /> Obviously there's more to the Facet than that, since we cover eg what happens in a Clash of Wills against a supernatural power that's tracking the Uratha (suffice to say that a Clash of Wills takes place but Feet of Mist is rather likely to win out).</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, awesome, awesome. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> A bit of a tangent, but very important to the chronicle I'm running/planning as we speak: what other tricks would be available for Uratha trying to pass themselves off as one of the Herd (like really deep cover agents)? That is, only if you can spill. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's getting even more difficult to wait for the book to finally come out. I just hope they'll be able to deliver to my area. XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3702,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","user":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","date":". 09-06-2014, 11:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","name":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T15:05:34-08:00","id":349325,"title":"","content":"It's Christmas! And with Christmas comes a seasonal spoiler!<br /> <br /> Santa Claws, werewolf gift-giver and sole member of the Lodge of Seasonal Cheer, uses various Gifts to make his life easier. Which would you like to know about?<br /> <br /> When it comes to knowing whether his prey... er, the good children have been good or have been bad, and whether they deserve Claws' particular brand of presents, he uses <b>Prey on Weakness</b> (Insight, Cunning) and <b>Know Thy Prey </b>(Knowledge, Cunning).<br /> <br /> No-one ever catches a glimpse of Santa Claws when he comes to place fetishes and talens under the tree-spirit. How does he manage this? Well, the <b>Lore of the Land</b> (Knowledge, Purity) and <b>Running Silent</b> (Stealth, Wisdom) Facets help out.<br /> <br /> Where Santa Claws passes, the weather should be appropriately snowy and the people should all be tucked away snug in their warm houses, hiding from the frigid, predatory, hungry cold that gnaws at the bone to the very marrow, calls the soul to oblivion and chills the... <i>ahem</i>. Er. People should all be at home by the fire, not out in the snow, because symbolism, see? When weather and people fail to co-operate, Claws uses the <b>Hunt of Fire and Ice</b> (Weather, Wisdom) and <b> All Doors Locked</b> (Warding, Honor) to damn well make them comply.<br /> <br /> Santa Claws has brought <i>you </i>a special Gift, so wrap up warm and make sure you leave out the fresh steak by the tree-spirit.<br /> <br /> <br /> Place your votes on which of the above-mentioned Facets you'd like to know more about, and I'll see if Santa Claws can't leave word of just how the most popular Facet works...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T16:03:53-08:00","id":349377,"title":"","content":"Let's hear about <b>Hunt of Fire and Ice</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-24-2014, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://foru